1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,060
[nm]: Let's talk about upādāna

2
00:00:02,708 --> 00:00:03,780
[kc]: Okay. Yeah.

3
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:08,571
[nm]: The... I think you're probably going to revolve around the same thing.

4
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:11,882
[nm]: [?Whatever], we can start...

5
00:00:14,757 --> 00:00:17,685
[nm]: Obviously, it's translated differently, and we are not getting into that.

6
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:28,682
[nm]: We usually regard it as assumption, because in its nature, you... If people thinks upādāna is attaching... Or what's the other one? Clinging.

7
00:00:29,334 --> 00:00:29,940
[kc]: Grasping.

8
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:36,128
[nm]: Grasping. Again, it implies me reacting to things in a certain appropriative manner.

9
00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:39,117
[nm]: But upādāna is what precedes that.

10
00:00:39,731 --> 00:00:43,634
[nm]: You appropriating things in regards of your mind is the result of the upādāna.

11
00:00:43,814 --> 00:00:44,922
[nm]: It's not your upādāna.

12
00:00:45,431 --> 00:00:49,560
[nm]: In other words, you can't... it's not on the level of choice for you to stop clinging.

13
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:57,980
[nm]: So, that's why whenever you say clinging or grasping, well, at least for me, it kind of sounds like, oh, I'm clinging to this and I'm grasping that.

14
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:58,600
[kc]: Yeah, to stop.

15
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,150
[nm]: And that's already the result of upādāna.

16
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:02,225
[nm]: That's what I mean: it's more of an assumption.

17
00:01:02,685 --> 00:01:03,830
[nm]: You took something for granted.

18
00:01:03,830 --> 00:01:10,570
[nm]: You took for granted that you can own this and now you're exercising your attitude and actions towards ownership.

19
00:01:11,110 --> 00:01:17,597
[nm]: But you will never do that if you fully understand that it's unownable to begin with, if you free yourself from that assumption.

20
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:30,542
[nm]: So, if we take assumption then, for the contemplation, what would be... how would you describe its properties?

21
00:01:31,048 --> 00:01:37,122
[nm]: Say... Well, let's practically... sensuality is an assumption.

22
00:01:39,225 --> 00:01:41,337
[nm]: So, how would you describe that?

23
00:01:42,071 --> 00:01:43,751
[nm]: Why is it an assumption?

24
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:52,854
[kc]: Well, for me, assumptions about, like, something that's unexamined...

25
00:02:02,745 --> 00:02:05,990
[kc]: that kind of underlies everything.

26
00:02:12,582 --> 00:02:15,162
[kc]: So, I guess, in terms of sensuality, it would be

27
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:19,342
[kc]: which is not understanding, not seeing, not examining.

28
00:02:19,794 --> 00:02:20,357
[nm]: What?

29
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:22,340
[kc]: What sensuality is.

30
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:24,468
[nm]: So, what is it?

31
00:02:28,262 --> 00:02:28,982
[tn]: Sensuality...?

32
00:02:29,194 --> 00:02:29,600
[nm]: Hmm.

33
00:02:29,857 --> 00:02:30,588
[tn]: or assumption?

34
00:02:31,328 --> 00:02:36,222
[nm]: You have... You arrive at assumption through the example of that which being assumed, in this case, sensuality.

35
00:02:36,251 --> 00:02:37,511
[nm]: So, what is sensuality then?

36
00:02:44,691 --> 00:02:57,305
[kc]: Your kind of... attitude towards things that you can bodily...

37
00:02:57,351 --> 00:03:01,562
[nm]: But don't, like, again, let's try and be more accurate in a sense of don't...

38
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:05,911
[nm]: There's no need for a theoretical answer.

39
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:09,922
[nm]: More like, imagine you... in the experience of sensuality,

40
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,502
[nm]: Craving for a taste...

41
00:03:11,974 --> 00:03:14,088
[kc]: So, feeling pulled towards something that I can taste.

42
00:03:14,088 --> 00:03:14,488
[nm]: Yeah, so, describe that.
[kc]: So, feeling pulled towards something that I can taste.

43
00:03:14,488 --> 00:03:15,300
[nm]: Yeah, so, describe that.

44
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:17,285
[nm]: So, it's a form of pull.

45
00:03:17,442 --> 00:03:17,705
[kc]: Yeah.

46
00:03:19,777 --> 00:03:28,751
[nm]: Can you have sensuality, for example, without a... without a desire?

47
00:03:30,702 --> 00:03:30,994
[kc]: No.

48
00:03:31,174 --> 00:03:37,742
[kc]: I think, to be honest, I think kāma comes from the verb kāmeti, which means desire.

49
00:03:39,031 --> 00:03:40,071
[kc]: It's just desire.

50
00:03:40,070 --> 00:03:40,500
[kc]: That's what it is.

51
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:41,311
[kc]: It's sense desire.

52
00:03:41,577 --> 00:03:42,062
[kc]: It's desire.

53
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:43,748
[nm]: Yeah, it's desire of the senses...

54
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,602
[kc]: Yeah, yeah, yeah. Something of the senses.

55
00:03:46,217 --> 00:03:58,890
[nm]: So you cannot possibly engage in any experience of sensuality, let's still call it sensuality, without having a desire underlying it.

56
00:04:00,725 --> 00:04:03,865
[nm]: So then, the assumption of sensuality must be on that level as well.

57
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:08,574
[kc]: On the level of desire.

58
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:15,868
[nm]: But as we described before, sensuality means perverting order of things.

59
00:04:16,431 --> 00:04:16,760
[nm]: Sorry.

60
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,300
[nm]: Assumption means.

61
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,320
[nm]: Upādāna means perverting order of things.

62
00:04:20,397 --> 00:04:21,722
[nm]: Owning the unownable.

63
00:04:22,422 --> 00:04:29,262
[nm]: Assuming the sense of self outside of this experience as a whole, which is a contradiction in terms, because you're experiencing that.

64
00:04:30,194 --> 00:04:39,988
[nm]: So, you maintaining an assumption whereby you think you can think outside of the experience as a whole, that's why it's an assumption.

65
00:04:41,917 --> 00:04:43,860
[nm]: Because it cannot be done,

66
00:04:44,434 --> 00:04:48,671
[nm]: yet, you not clarifying that it cannot be done, you keep doing it.

67
00:04:49,154 --> 00:05:00,625
[nm]: So then, the desire, being also another type of upādāna, shares the same nature, or must be sharing the same nature.

68
00:05:00,888 --> 00:05:09,202
[kc]: Isn't it because desire basically involves this given situation?

69
00:05:10,482 --> 00:05:19,185
[kc]: I mean, this, this basically, like, so: I, sitting here, not having this taste, but with that taste as a possibility.

70
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:25,168
[nm]: Let's make it even more... narrow.

71
00:05:25,474 --> 00:05:25,834
[kc]: Okay.

72
00:05:26,497 --> 00:05:28,474
[nm]: Would you have desire if things are unpleasant?

73
00:05:29,968 --> 00:05:30,254
[kc]: No.

74
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,425
[kc]: That's it.

75
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,020
[kc]: So it's a desire.

76
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:32,220
[nm]: Pleasure.

77
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:32,588
[kc]: Pleasure.

78
00:05:32,709 --> 00:05:32,909
[kc]: Yeah.

79
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:35,310
[nm]: It's a desire for pleasure.

80
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:35,425
[kc]: Yeah.

81
00:05:35,968 --> 00:05:39,542
[nm]: And then, is that the pleasure also basis for your desire?

82
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:46,562
[kc]: The pleasure for... Wanting pleasure is the basis for the desire.

83
00:05:47,608 --> 00:05:51,505
[nm]: How would you be wanting pleasure, unless that's already felt pleasantly?

84
00:05:53,594 --> 00:05:56,230
[nm]: How would you know it's pleasant, unless you're feeling it pleasantly?

85
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:56,657
[kc]: Yeah, that's the thing.

86
00:05:56,650 --> 00:05:57,691
[kc]: That's what I wanted to say.

87
00:05:57,751 --> 00:06:02,674
[kc]: That basically, the possibility of pleasure is given to me.

88
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:07,217
[kc]: It's basically: I have been subjected to this...

89
00:06:08,042 --> 00:06:18,485
[kc]: This possibility for pleasure, not seeing that that possibility for pleasure is just something else that I've been subjected to, I think, let's go for...

90
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,288
[kc]: I want to go for that.

91
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,388
[nm]: And how is that possibility of pleasure felt?

92
00:06:22,485 --> 00:06:25,940
[kc]: That... [?Let] that possibility of... well, it depends.

93
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:32,868
[kc]: If it's not recognized as something that I've just been subjected to, then it'll be felt as pleasant.

94
00:06:33,148 --> 00:06:37,148
[kc]: But if you see that it's just yet another thing that I've been subjected to,

95
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:48,151
[kc]: just like this lack of that... this feeling I have, not having that thing, whether I'm subjected to that feeling or that feeling, it's all just...

96
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:52,910
[kc]: If you...

97
00:06:52,910 --> 00:07:00,880
[kc]: I think if you recognize it on the level of... on that level of it's all just something that I have been hit with, then...

98
00:07:01,531 --> 00:07:03,622
[kc]: You see the pain of pleasure.

99
00:07:03,830 --> 00:07:04,540
[nm ]: Sure, sure.

100
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:08,528
[nm]: But I'm not talking about like, oh, when you made the effort to recognize it.

101
00:07:08,710 --> 00:07:11,911
[nm]: Just the experience of the arisen prospect of pleasure.

102
00:07:12,470 --> 00:07:13,531
[nm]: How's that felt?

103
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:17,617
[kc]: The experience of the arisen prospect of pleasure? So, that's pleasurable.

104
00:07:17,991 --> 00:07:18,865
[nm]: Sensual pleasure, yeah.

105
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:26,250
[nm]: So, so you're not engaging, your senses are not engaging with particular pleasure, but now there is a possibility for them to do so.

106
00:07:26,252 --> 00:07:26,412
[kc]: Yeah.

107
00:07:26,682 --> 00:07:27,530
[nm]: How's that felt?

108
00:07:27,532 --> 00:07:28,473
[kc]: That's felt pleasurable.

109
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:33,577
[kc]: Well, actually, no, it's felt as painful, in the sense that: I'm, I want, I need to do this.

110
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:35,685
[kc]: But there's a pleasure involved in that.

111
00:07:36,402 --> 00:07:36,977
[nm]: Exactly.

112
00:07:37,010 --> 00:07:39,002
[nm]: But which, which is the one that comes first?

113
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:39,954
[kc]: Which is the one that comes first?

114
00:07:40,150 --> 00:07:43,359
[kc]: Well, as it's always important... It depends how you see it.

115
00:07:43,350 --> 00:07:45,585
[kc]: So, if you, if you don't recognize,

116
00:07:46,528 --> 00:07:47,580
[kc]: if you don't see...

117
00:07:47,830 --> 00:07:49,548
[nm]: No, it doesn't depend, like it...

118
00:07:50,045 --> 00:07:56,960
[nm]: Like, as I explained about the upādāna of attāvada, for example: it doesn't depend how you see it.

119
00:07:57,120 --> 00:08:02,320
[nm]: You always keep assuming your sense of self outside of the experience as a whole, outside of the five aggregates.

120
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,697
[nm]: Whether you see it or not, it doesn't matter.

121
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,420
[nm]: That's the mistake.

122
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:09,068
[nm]: So, once you start seeing it, you undo it, and then there is no other way.

123
00:08:09,708 --> 00:08:12,968
[nm]: You can't assume it again, because now you saw it as impossible.

124
00:08:14,697 --> 00:08:17,131
[nm]: So, sense-desire shares the same nature.

125
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:19,617
[nm]: So, that's what we're trying to get to the bottom of.

126
00:08:20,671 --> 00:08:22,288
[nm]: Where is that nature contained?

127
00:08:22,988 --> 00:08:24,357
[kc]: So, what was the question again?

128
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:25,400
[kc]: So, what...

129
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:36,000
[nm]: So, which is... which is that which comes first in the case of arisen prospect of sensual desire, or rather sensual pursuit, sensual pleasure?

130
00:08:36,677 --> 00:08:38,962
[nm]: Is it that it's unpleasant first,

131
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:47,200
[nm]: and then prospect of pleasure comes over it, or prospect of pleasure is first, but then that's felt unpleasantly.

132
00:08:48,494 --> 00:08:49,134
[nm]: Which one is it?

133
00:08:52,522 --> 00:08:54,851
[nm]: Again, let's back to the practical example.

134
00:08:54,920 --> 00:09:03,528
[nm]: Go back to... You have now possibility for a pleasant taste, to eat something.

135
00:09:05,308 --> 00:09:06,514
[nm]: How is that felt?

136
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:15,980
[kc]: I guess, like, ordinarily, it would be pleasurable.

137
00:09:16,491 --> 00:09:16,982
[nm]: Okay.

138
00:09:17,050 --> 00:09:22,040
[kc]: But now when you start thinking about it... Now when you start thinking about it, you realize that, well, there's a pain involved in not having it.

139
00:09:23,928 --> 00:09:25,280
[nm]: And which is... that comes first?

140
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:27,470
[nm]: Is it the pain or the ordinary...?

141
00:09:27,470 --> 00:09:28,780
[kc]: Which is more fundamental? Is the pain.

142
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:29,120
[nm]: Exactly.

143
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,065
[kc]: That's the [?anything else is the] more fundamental.

144
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:32,502
[nm]: So, the pain is more fundamental.

145
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:33,060
[kc]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

146
00:09:33,534 --> 00:09:34,708
[nm]: The absence of pleasure.

147
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:42,140
[kc]: The absence of pleasure, right now, is... that is... that's more fundamental than the initial kind of buzz you get from the possibility.

148
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:42,454
[nm]: Yeah.

149
00:09:42,728 --> 00:09:51,368
[nm]: So, if the absence of this possible pleasure, this particular food, is first felt unpleasantlh...

150
00:09:54,471 --> 00:09:59,277
[nm]: what would be the necessary basis, then, for you to go for that pleasure?

151
00:09:59,650 --> 00:10:03,897
[kc]: To not see that pain.

152
00:10:04,314 --> 00:10:05,174
[kc]: To cover over it.

153
00:10:05,374 --> 00:10:06,730
[nm]: Sure, to cover over it, yeah.

154
00:10:07,214 --> 00:10:13,670
[nm]: So, in that way, any form of engagement of sense desires requires you to ignore how you feel first.

155
00:10:13,670 --> 00:10:13,925
[kc]: Yeah.

156
00:10:14,797 --> 00:10:16,450
[nm]: Of the fundamental feeling. Okay.

157
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:16,868
[kc]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

158
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:23,100
[nm]: So, the pathway of following the sense desire is always open.

159
00:10:24,070 --> 00:10:25,077
[nm]: There's nothing blocking it.

160
00:10:25,850 --> 00:10:29,322
[nm]: But the fact is that that's felt unpleasantly first.

161
00:10:29,937 --> 00:10:32,888
[nm]: And you ignore it, in order to go down that way.

162
00:10:33,217 --> 00:10:34,531
[nm]: That's why it's a mistake.

163
00:10:34,530 --> 00:10:34,780
[kc]: Okay.

164
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:39,702
[kc]: Can I say it's like... it's... you're saying it's first felt as unpleasant.

165
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:40,490
[nm]: Fundamentally, yeah.

166
00:10:40,490 --> 00:10:43,677
[kc]: Can I say it's like it's more... the more general feeling?

167
00:10:43,808 --> 00:10:44,100
[nm]: Oh, yeah.

168
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:47,891
[nm]: I don't mean first felt as in that when you chase the pleasure, the pain disappears.

169
00:10:47,890 --> 00:10:49,280
[kc]: So, there is... there is a pleasure...

170
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:53,420
[nm]: The pain remains throughout, which is why the pain is the motivation of your sensuality.

171
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:54,914
[kc]: So, it's like there's a pleasure...

172
00:10:55,428 --> 00:11:04,251
[kc]: the... this buzz of the possibility of having that taste, but that pleasure is contained within this more general displeasure. It's more...

173
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:04,660
[nm]: Sure.

174
00:11:04,848 --> 00:11:06,825
[nm]: Yeah, that's what I keep talking about more fundamental.

175
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:07,068
[kc]: Yeah.

176
00:11:08,091 --> 00:11:17,945
[nm]: So, the more fundamental discomfort of the prospect of pleasure remains throughout your engagement with the pleasure, which is why you keep engaging with the pleasure.

177
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:23,870
[kc]: So, not being mindful would help you to ignore that more fundamental pain.

178
00:11:23,870 --> 00:11:24,420
[nm]: Yeah.

179
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:25,334
[nm]: Well, that's the thing.

180
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:30,174
[nm]: There is no starting point for the ignorance in regard to anything, including sensuality.

181
00:11:30,762 --> 00:11:44,271
[nm]: And because there is no starting point of this type of ignoring, people... there is also no starting point for their assumption that prospect of pleasure is the pleasure that they already delight in, that they engage with, that they pursue, and so on.

182
00:11:44,974 --> 00:11:48,997
[nm]: So, they don't see the underlying pain that's constantly present with it.

183
00:11:49,671 --> 00:11:52,845
[nm]: Simultaneously, to the same extent, but on a more fundamental level.

184
00:11:53,234 --> 00:12:01,011
[nm]: So then, through your own engagement with sensuality, you keep obscuring more and more that which underlines it, which is pain.

185
00:12:02,445 --> 00:12:05,142
[nm]: And that's why sensuality is insatiable.

186
00:12:06,048 --> 00:12:08,771
[nm]: Because pain is here, on one level.

187
00:12:09,177 --> 00:12:12,782
[nm]: Your act towards sensuality alone can be on the domain of sensuality.

188
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:17,294
[nm]: It cannot do anything about the fact that it's felt painfully before you act.

189
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:29,962
[nm]: So, then, no amount of action, satisfaction, desire, proliferation, the extent of your even sensual preferences... Yeah, no amount of restraint would then automatically...

190
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:36,614
[nm]: Obviously, restraint is necessary, for you to start, then, questioning backwards, so to speak, and not keep chasing the senses objects.

191
00:12:36,870 --> 00:12:38,582
[kc]: But if I'd say it's that more general level...

192
00:12:38,580 --> 00:12:42,310
[nm]: No. Unless you understand it, you won't be free from it.

193
00:12:42,310 --> 00:12:49,394
[nm]: Because, again, sensuality is not engagement with the objects of your senses.

194
00:12:49,568 --> 00:12:51,265
[nm]: Sensuality is assumption.

195
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:52,605
[nm]: It's an upādāna.

196
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:58,094
[nm]: Which means, there is some perversion of the order there, that's why sensuality is there.

197
00:12:58,291 --> 00:13:02,431
[nm]: Now, that perversion is maintained through your engagement based on that ignorance.

198
00:13:02,971 --> 00:13:04,270
[nm]: Engagement with sense-objects.

199
00:13:04,270 --> 00:13:10,125
[nm]: But, once you remove the ignorance, then engagement with sense-objects cannot induce sensuality anymore.

200
00:13:10,262 --> 00:13:17,217
[nm]: But, that obviously means that the extent of your old engagement that was based on ignorance will be significantly reduced.

201
00:13:17,611 --> 00:13:20,257
[nm]: Such as, arahant cannot possibly have sexual intercourse.

202
00:13:21,322 --> 00:13:25,800
[nm]: Or think about sensual thoughts: oh, I want, I am going to eat the next day, and then this... Just unthinkeable for him.

203
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:30,017
[nm]: But now, let's make it even more accurate.

204
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:42,194
[nm]: If sensualities first felt unpleasantly... let's, don't think about the prospect of the pleasure, now,

205
00:13:42,437 --> 00:13:43,680
[nm]: just think about the pain.

206
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:45,090
[nm]: Since we revealed it.

207
00:13:45,090 --> 00:13:45,297
[kc]: Yeah.

208
00:13:46,042 --> 00:13:46,445
[nm]: How...

209
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:48,077
[kc]: I'm not having this thing that I could have.

210
00:13:48,097 --> 00:13:48,634
[nm]: Any pain.

211
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:48,988
[kc]: Yeah.

212
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:51,440
[nm]: Any nature of painful feeling.

213
00:13:51,445 --> 00:13:51,710
[kc]: Yeah.

214
00:13:52,474 --> 00:13:54,440
[nm]: What are its characteristics?

215
00:13:55,730 --> 00:13:56,500
[kc]: Painful feeling.

216
00:13:59,445 --> 00:14:06,474
[nm]: Or what are the characteristics of the experience as a whole that is subjected to a painful feeling that endures?

217
00:14:12,954 --> 00:14:16,320
[kc]: That it's something that you are subjected to.

218
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:17,917
[nm]: Okay.

219
00:14:19,348 --> 00:14:25,000
[kc]: So, I can only discover that pain as already enjoying.

220
00:14:26,248 --> 00:14:27,100
[kc]: What else do you discover?

221
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:28,671
[kc]: I have no control over it being there.

222
00:14:29,408 --> 00:14:29,842
[nm]: Okay.

223
00:14:30,314 --> 00:14:33,574
[nm]: So, what is the natural response?

224
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:41,425
[kc]: So, the ordinary response would be, if you were to not understand that that pain isn't yours, the ordinary response is to say, I don't want that.

225
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:44,390
[nm]: Well, what would be a non-anāgāmī response?

226
00:14:44,390 --> 00:14:45,151
[nm]: I don't want that.

227
00:14:45,457 --> 00:14:45,845
[nm]: Yeah.

228
00:14:45,997 --> 00:14:47,110
[nm]: So, not wanting pain.

229
00:14:47,110 --> 00:14:47,291
[kc]: Yeah.

230
00:14:48,465 --> 00:14:49,511
[tn]: It's undesirable.

231
00:14:50,048 --> 00:14:50,660
[nm]: Exactly.

232
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:54,597
[kc]: But that's only because you're not recognizing that it's got... Yeah, no, that's fine.

233
00:14:54,590 --> 00:14:56,280
[nm]: Yeah. No, that's fine, that's fine.

234
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:59,331
[nm]: Let's just stick with the pain, because it's basically undesirable.

235
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:03,068
[nm]: And as the Buddha said, in every painful feeling, there is craving to get rid of it.

236
00:15:03,911 --> 00:15:05,600
[nm]: Unless you're completely free from craving.

237
00:15:08,050 --> 00:15:11,465
[nm]: And how is that prospect of getting rid of pain felt?

238
00:15:11,625 --> 00:15:12,080
[kc]: Painfully.

239
00:15:12,928 --> 00:15:13,314
[nm]: Is it?

240
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:14,620
[kc]: Oh, I see.

241
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:15,025
[kc]: Okay.

242
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:15,751
[kc]: Oh, well.

243
00:15:16,882 --> 00:15:19,790
[nm]: So, you're subjected to pain and there is a possibility of pain ceasing.

244
00:15:19,790 --> 00:15:20,110
[kc]: Pleasing.

245
00:15:20,110 --> 00:15:20,728
[kc]: No, no, no. Okay

246
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:24,745
[kc]: So, the possibility of that pain not being there is felt pleasant.

247
00:15:25,068 --> 00:15:25,771
[nm]: Felt pleasantly.

248
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:28,168
[nm]: What is the pleasure of that prospect?

249
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:28,670
[nm]: I'm just thinking as...

250
00:15:28,670 --> 00:15:29,530
[nm]: Hold on. Hold on. Hold on.

251
00:15:29,530 --> 00:15:30,290
[nm]: We're on a thread here.

252
00:15:30,298 --> 00:15:30,618
[kc]: Okay.

253
00:15:31,070 --> 00:15:36,057
[nm]: What is then the pleasure in that prospect?

254
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:37,351
[nm]: What is pleasant?

255
00:15:37,768 --> 00:15:39,025
[kc]: Of that pain not being there...

256
00:15:39,845 --> 00:15:48,540
[nm]: So, then, the pleasure of the prospect of not having this pain is pleasant to the extent that this is painful.

257
00:15:49,228 --> 00:15:49,600
[kc]: Yes.

258
00:15:50,425 --> 00:15:51,997
[nm]: It's not a separate pleasure.

259
00:15:52,802 --> 00:15:53,105
[kc]: No.

260
00:15:53,351 --> 00:15:54,877
[nm]: It's a back of the same coin.

261
00:15:54,922 --> 00:15:55,374
[kc]: It is.

262
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:55,940
[kc]: Yeah.

263
00:15:56,811 --> 00:15:57,650
[nm]: So, it's one phenomenon.

264
00:15:57,657 --> 00:15:59,478
[kc]: It's another way of looking at the... it's the one thing.

265
00:15:59,470 --> 00:16:00,877
[nm]: It's one phenomenon there.

266
00:16:01,039 --> 00:16:01,219
[kc]: Yeah.

267
00:16:01,308 --> 00:16:04,242
[nm]: Because every presence of this implies the absence of this.

268
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:05,100
[nm]: Whatever that is.

269
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:05,405
[kc]: Yeah.

270
00:16:05,565 --> 00:16:08,600
[nm]: So, presence of pain implies absence of pain.

271
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:08,820
[kc]: Yeah.

272
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:09,680
[nm]: This same pain.

273
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:10,217
[kc]: Yeah, yeah, yeah...

274
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:14,008
[nm]: Presence of pain is felt unpleasantly.

275
00:16:14,414 --> 00:16:18,780
[nm]: Simultaneous to that, the possibility of its absence is felt pleasantly.

276
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:19,048
[kc]: Yeah.

277
00:16:19,631 --> 00:16:20,292
[nm]: Just an [?episode] of that.

278
00:16:20,290 --> 00:16:24,665
[nm]: And that pain and that possibility of pleasure are they separate?

279
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:25,908
[kc]: Completely bound up with each other.

280
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:26,528
[nm]: Exactly.

281
00:16:27,094 --> 00:16:27,360
[kc]: Yeah.

282
00:16:27,462 --> 00:16:33,760
[nm]: So, if you look at one, yeah, you can say that's what I'm feeling, but if you look at the other, but again, from where do they come from?

283
00:16:33,834 --> 00:16:35,110
[nm]: They come from the same thing.

284
00:16:35,116 --> 00:16:35,416
[kc]: Yeah.

285
00:16:36,210 --> 00:16:38,417
[kc]: That you've been struck by that feeling.

286
00:16:38,482 --> 00:16:38,811
[nm]: Yeah.

287
00:16:39,174 --> 00:16:42,877
[nm]: So, it's basically one phenomena with two sides.

288
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:43,440
[kc]: Yeah.

289
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:45,937
[nm]: Like two sides of one coin, literally.

290
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:48,571
[nm]: So, you can't have one without having the other.

291
00:16:48,682 --> 00:16:48,900
[kc]: Yeah.

292
00:16:49,797 --> 00:16:52,554
[nm]: And it's on that level that sensuality happens.

293
00:16:53,328 --> 00:16:54,294
[nm]: The assumption of it.

294
00:16:56,771 --> 00:16:57,734
[kc]: So, you...

295
00:16:57,730 --> 00:16:58,991
[nm]: The wrong order.

296
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,140
[kc]: So, You put the negative...

297
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:01,340
[nm]: The outside in regard to this.

298
00:17:01,340 --> 00:17:02,810
[kc]: Yeah. You put the negative first.

299
00:17:02,810 --> 00:17:04,017
[nm]:  Well, you put the pleasure first.

300
00:17:04,010 --> 00:17:05,174
[kc]: Yeah, yeah, yeah. Yeah.

301
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:06,022
[nm]: Completely gratuitous.

302
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:07,137
[kc]: Whatever place it's absolutely... yeah.

303
00:17:07,130 --> 00:17:17,337
[nm]: In case ot attāvada, you put that first because it's more pleasant, because it shelters you from the daily [?onwards] of anxiety, that you are not in control of your life, you are not in control of your senses.

304
00:17:17,490 --> 00:17:25,402
[nm]: So, you assume the external point of view to this experience of a whole that's kind of unaffected, despite whatever is happening in this experience.

305
00:17:25,648 --> 00:17:35,291
[nm]: But that's a completely gratuitous assumption that's almost like developed for the purpose of kind of covering it up, covering the issues up, a defense mechanism, so to speak.

306
00:17:36,368 --> 00:17:40,948
[nm]: And that's that's always the principle of every upādāna, by the way; avoiding pain.

307
00:17:41,354 --> 00:17:46,600
[nm]: That's why you develop assumptions, because they shelter you from admitting that you are subject to pain.

308
00:17:48,054 --> 00:17:52,162
[nm]: We can go into the other upādānas as well, and you'll see it's going to be the same principle.

309
00:17:53,371 --> 00:17:59,322
[nm]: Like sīlabbataparāmāsa, my virtue, my duty, not my responsibility to make it my virtue, my duty.

310
00:18:00,190 --> 00:18:01,788
[tn]: Can we stay with sensuality?

311
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:02,150
[tn]: Yeah, yeah.

312
00:18:02,150 --> 00:18:04,717
[nm]: I'm just, I'm just dropping this in, so you can connect.

313
00:18:04,910 --> 00:18:05,302
[kc]: Okay.

314
00:18:05,370 --> 00:18:07,142
[nm]: But let's go back to the thread that we said.

315
00:18:07,194 --> 00:18:09,470
[nm]: So, the two sides of the same coin.

316
00:18:09,470 --> 00:18:12,474
[kc]: Can I just say, so it would be the same if there's a pleasant feeling?

317
00:18:13,202 --> 00:18:13,611
[tn]: Yeah.

318
00:18:13,710 --> 00:18:14,768
[kc]: That pleasant feeling.

319
00:18:15,317 --> 00:18:18,880
[kc]: The presence of the pleasant feeling implies the lack of that pleasant feeling.

320
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:19,185
[nm]: Yeah.

321
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:20,200
[kc]: Which would be painful.

322
00:18:21,402 --> 00:18:22,214
[nm]: And you assume that.

323
00:18:22,210 --> 00:18:25,751
[kc] But, you and you assume... but you...

324
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:28,188
[nm]: You put the possibility.

325
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:32,937
[kc]: But generally, one would emphasize the pleasure and ignore... No.

326
00:18:32,930 --> 00:18:37,970
[nm]: No. See, like, again, imagine practically you're subjected to some sensual pleasure right now.

327
00:18:37,970 --> 00:18:38,262
[kc]: Yeah.

328
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:42,360
[nm]: It takes effort for you to not crave for more of it.

329
00:18:42,590 --> 00:18:48,302
[nm]: It takes effort for you to go against the grain and stay and appreciate what you have and enjoy it.

330
00:18:48,671 --> 00:18:51,917
[nm]: Because if you don't make the effort, the mind wants more.

331
00:18:52,648 --> 00:18:55,842
[nm]: Because more pleasure means this is painful.

332
00:18:56,991 --> 00:18:57,480
[nm]: Same.

333
00:18:57,637 --> 00:18:58,765
[nm]: Pain is painful.

334
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:01,928
[nm]: Absence of pain is more pleasurable.

335
00:19:02,337 --> 00:19:04,562
[nm]: You put that absence of pain first.

336
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,482
[nm]: On the basis, within the container of that it's painful first.

337
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:14,880
[nm]: So, that's why... that's why we started by asking in general what is first in case of sensuality.

338
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,448
[nm]: It's always... that is its container.

339
00:19:16,757 --> 00:19:18,697
[nm]: That is its fundamental purpose.

340
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:36,565
[nm]: And then you realize that no amount of engagement with sensuality, as I said, doesn't matter how far down the senses you go, the motivation, the actual pleasure that you feel, on account of sensual engagement, is the pleasure of avoiding pain that's still with you.

341
00:19:37,062 --> 00:19:41,211
[nm]: Not the pleasure of you touching things, tasting things.

342
00:19:41,488 --> 00:19:48,317
[nm]: Because if the pleasure were contained in touch, taste, smell, sight,

343
00:19:49,130 --> 00:20:01,954
[nm]: it would always be pleasant to the same extent, and you wouldn't even... well, you wouldn't be able to think about it, to be honest, because not having... that means... non-engagement means absence of pleasure, absence of possibility of pleasure.

344
00:20:03,411 --> 00:20:16,962
[nm]: But the fact that sometimes you can eat same things and not experience pleasure on account of it, then eat... eat same things they used to... didn't cause you pleasure, now they're giving you pleasure, means pleasure is not in the sense objects, nor in the sense domain, for that matter.

345
00:20:17,948 --> 00:20:19,851
[nm]: And, of course, the Buddha said that many times.

346
00:20:20,391 --> 00:20:27,168
[nm]: Like, once you remove desire and lust from your mind, he said even Tathāgata... For Tathāgata, there are beautiful things in the world.

347
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:33,705
[nm]: He sees this is beautiful, this is ugly, this is agreeable, this is disagreeable, but there's absolutely no sensuality whatsoever.

348
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:41,302
[nm]: But for most people, when you think, you think sensuality means the the the agreeability of the sense objects.

349
00:20:41,945 --> 00:20:42,488
[nm]: But it doesn't.

350
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:44,782
[nm]: Sensuality means perversion of your perception.

351
00:20:44,834 --> 00:20:45,728
[kc]: An assumption, yeah.

352
00:20:45,814 --> 00:20:51,737
[nm]: You perceive second to come first, and that which is actually still there is first, you kind of perceive as second.

353
00:20:52,511 --> 00:20:56,442
[nm]: And from that point of view, you realize how sensuality is not linear at all.

354
00:20:57,360 --> 00:21:01,948
[nm]: Because usually it's like the mind would, once it's subjected to that assumption,

355
00:21:02,731 --> 00:21:10,837
[nm]: and acts out of the assumption would think, I have a desire, then I act, then I fulfill my desire through engaging with this particular sense object.

356
00:21:11,474 --> 00:21:12,474
[nm]: And then it's done.

357
00:21:13,620 --> 00:21:18,391
[nm]: The whole thing is within the painful container of being subjected to it in the first place.

358
00:21:18,862 --> 00:21:20,365
[nm]: And that is your sole motivation.

359
00:21:22,908 --> 00:21:34,970
[nm]: But the important precision here is, whenever there is a prospect of pleasure that's felt pleasantly, because you'll be avoiding pain, that pleasure is the pleasure of the pain that you're feeling.

360
00:21:34,970 --> 00:21:35,211
[nm]: Yeah.

361
00:21:35,565 --> 00:21:42,777
[kc]: So, that's why you should learn to see sensuality, sense desires... as

362
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:44,865
[nm]: As perillous.

363
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:46,968
[kc]: charocal, painful.

364
00:21:47,214 --> 00:21:47,757
[nm]: Sure.

365
00:21:49,045 --> 00:21:58,220
[nm]: Now that you brought it up, the Buddha will always say he understands, the one who is free from sensuality, understands gratification, the danger and the escape.

366
00:21:58,580 --> 00:22:00,300
[nm]: That means full understanding of the phenomenon.

367
00:22:01,825 --> 00:22:05,117
[nm]: So, what is then the gratification of the sensual assumption?

368
00:22:05,805 --> 00:22:07,308
[kc]: The pleasure that...

369
00:22:07,382 --> 00:22:08,077
[nm]: Which pleasure?

370
00:22:11,530 --> 00:22:17,314
[kc]: The gratification... well, the extent of the pleasure that you can possibly... that is contained within that pain.

371
00:22:18,990 --> 00:22:21,094
[nm]: The extent of the pleasure that's contained with the pain?

372
00:22:21,090 --> 00:22:22,714
[kc]: Yeah, so, so, basically...

373
00:22:22,710 --> 00:22:24,640
[nm]: But that it's... I mean, that extent would be quite infinite.

374
00:22:26,514 --> 00:22:29,697
[kc]: No, because it's all within more general pain.

375
00:22:30,028 --> 00:22:34,405
[kc]: So, there is a pleasure there, a more particular pleasure, which is what you're putting first.

376
00:22:34,868 --> 00:22:40,151
[kc]: Sorry, what somebody, you know, somebody who's bound by sensuality, puts first, this pleasure.

377
00:22:41,088 --> 00:22:44,310
[kc]: Not seeing that that's bound up by a more fundamental pain.

378
00:22:44,310 --> 00:22:45,602
[nm]: Yeah, but what is gratification?

379
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:46,271
[kc]: That pleasure.

380
00:22:46,270 --> 00:22:51,114
[kc]: And how... the extent to which that can... the way...

381
00:22:51,297 --> 00:22:55,017
[nm]: So, the gratification, then, is absence of pain.

382
00:22:55,790 --> 00:22:57,720
[kc]: The gratification is absence of pain.

383
00:23:04,902 --> 00:23:06,162
[kc]: [??]. [nm]: [?So, it's a pleasure in pain?]

384
00:23:06,257 --> 00:23:08,582
[kc]: It's because it's a pain... there's a pleasure there.

385
00:23:10,288 --> 00:23:12,397
[kc]: You know, you have this prospect of pleasure.

386
00:23:12,777 --> 00:23:13,650
[nm]: So, let's put it like this.

387
00:23:13,650 --> 00:23:15,160
[nm]: Where is that gratification?

388
00:23:15,250 --> 00:23:16,430
[nm]: There is gratification.

389
00:23:16,430 --> 00:23:16,702
[kc]: Yeah.

390
00:23:16,734 --> 00:23:17,928
[nm]: And it needs to be understood.

391
00:23:18,098 --> 00:23:18,378
[kc]: Yeah.

392
00:23:18,574 --> 00:23:19,105
[nm]: Where is it?

393
00:23:24,368 --> 00:23:25,734
[nm]: Anybody can chip in, by the way.

394
00:23:26,694 --> 00:23:28,840
[tn]: Is it the ignoring of the pain?

395
00:23:30,531 --> 00:23:31,671
[tn]: The blindness to...

396
00:23:31,928 --> 00:23:33,342
[nm]: Ignoring of the pain.

397
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:36,411
[nm]: Well...

398
00:23:36,602 --> 00:23:37,585
[tn]: It's pleasurable, is

399
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:38,057
[nm]: Yeah.

400
00:23:38,128 --> 00:23:40,085
[nm]: But again, more, more precisely.

401
00:23:41,125 --> 00:23:43,311
[nm]: Now, we are not trying to undo the gratification.

402
00:23:43,531 --> 00:23:44,928
[nm]: We're just trying to clarify it.

403
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:45,571
[nm]: What is it?

404
00:23:46,310 --> 00:23:47,780
[nm]: Because there is gratification.

405
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:50,022
[kc]: It's the pleasure that arises on...

406
00:23:50,211 --> 00:23:50,911
[nm]: Okay. Yeah.

407
00:23:50,977 --> 00:23:52,345
[nm]: So, let's stop there.

408
00:23:52,340 --> 00:23:59,345
[nm]: The pleasure that arises on account of possibility of sense objects, which are, yeah, all of it is underlined by the pain.

409
00:23:59,405 --> 00:23:59,757
[nm]: Sure.

410
00:23:59,825 --> 00:24:00,097
[kc]: Yeah.

411
00:24:00,197 --> 00:24:05,734
[nm]: So, why is that pleasure pleasant, as I asked before, as we clarified before?

412
00:24:06,685 --> 00:24:09,397
[nm]: Why are you feeling that prospect pleasantly?

413
00:24:10,317 --> 00:24:14,711
[kc]: Because there's... because you're emphasizing...

414
00:24:17,022 --> 00:24:19,340
[nm]: Because you crave getting rid of the pain.

415
00:24:20,710 --> 00:24:22,382
[nm]: So, then, that's the gratification.

416
00:24:22,654 --> 00:24:26,668
[nm]: Delighting in the prospect of getting rid of the pain that you don't question.

417
00:24:27,320 --> 00:24:33,085
[nm]: So, you don't question your attitude towards the originally, fundamentally, presently enduring pain.

418
00:24:33,391 --> 00:24:34,354
[nm]: You don't question it,

419
00:24:35,074 --> 00:24:38,251
[nm]: then, there are prospects to then, like, get away from it,

420
00:24:38,417 --> 00:24:40,477
[nm]: and you will then automatically delight in it.

421
00:24:40,634 --> 00:24:41,531
[nm]: And that's what Buddha said:

422
00:24:41,610 --> 00:24:44,885
[nm]: Gratification is the delight, in sense objects.

423
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:47,180
[nm]: It's your delight in the sense object.

424
00:24:47,180 --> 00:24:48,745
[nm]: That's the gratification of sensuality.

425
00:24:48,740 --> 00:24:50,342
[nm]: Not engagement with the sense objects.

426
00:24:50,340 --> 00:24:51,980
[nm]: Even if you can get everything you want.

427
00:24:52,630 --> 00:24:54,677
[nm]: It's you delighting, that's were...

428
00:24:54,670 --> 00:24:58,042
[nm]: That's already when you start satisfying your desires.

429
00:24:58,568 --> 00:25:02,242
[nm]: Because you accept the possibility of satisfaction.

430
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:07,565
[nm]: As in, satisfaction over there, means escaping this presently enduring pain over here.

431
00:25:07,870 --> 00:25:09,151
[tn]: So, you could say, it's a hope...?

432
00:25:10,168 --> 00:25:11,594
[nm]: Yeah, sure, sure.

433
00:25:12,197 --> 00:25:13,620
[nm]: It's on that level, certainly.

434
00:25:13,620 --> 00:25:18,508
[nm]: You might not be explicitly thinking, like, clarifying: oh, it's a hope. But yeah, it's on that level.

435
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:20,320
[tn]: So, the possibility of satisfaction... ...is already delighted in.

436
00:25:21,062 --> 00:25:22,551
[nm]: is already delighted in.

437
00:25:22,748 --> 00:25:28,217
[nm]: That's already... that delight in the possibility of satisfaction is where gratification already is.

438
00:25:30,380 --> 00:25:31,228
[nm]: And the...

439
00:25:31,220 --> 00:25:32,965
[tn]: Well that, then the danger is made clear, right?

440
00:25:33,670 --> 00:25:34,528
[tn]: Exactly, yeah.

441
00:25:34,651 --> 00:25:39,588
[nm]: Because you go down the domain that has nothing to do with why you are going down that domain.

442
00:25:39,997 --> 00:25:43,808
[nm]: Because, again, there's a whole irony contained in any assumption.

443
00:25:45,100 --> 00:25:50,797
[nm]: This unpleasantly arisen experience as a whole... you don't want that pain.

444
00:25:51,885 --> 00:25:55,897
[nm]: So, by not wanting that pain, you go to that which is painful.

445
00:25:56,560 --> 00:26:02,230
[nm]: Because that unpleasant... unpleasant arisen experience, the whole is the experience of sensuality, as we described it.

446
00:26:03,274 --> 00:26:07,011
[nm]: Whenever there is a sense desire, it's first felt unpleasantly.

447
00:26:07,665 --> 00:26:12,060
[nm]: Because you don't want that unpleasure, you engage with it.

448
00:26:13,405 --> 00:26:15,097
[nm]: And then, how do you think it's going to be felt?

449
00:26:15,674 --> 00:26:16,488
[nm]: Unpleasantly.

450
00:26:16,982 --> 00:26:19,300
[nm]: So, literally, like scratching the itch, as the Buddha said.

451
00:26:19,300 --> 00:26:20,951
[nm]: Each time you engage, you make it worse.

452
00:26:21,554 --> 00:26:23,965
[nm]: So then, if you clarify this, you realize that

453
00:26:24,860 --> 00:26:28,708
[nm]: sensuality arises, and it's felt unpleasantly, and you don't want pain.

454
00:26:28,700 --> 00:26:29,751
[nm]: Nobody wants pain.

455
00:26:29,977 --> 00:26:36,848
[nm]: And then you realize sense restrain is then the pleasure... in regard to that painful sensuality.

456
00:26:38,308 --> 00:26:43,537
[nm]: Abstaining from engagement with sensuality is how you're going to free yourself from that pain of that sensuality.

457
00:26:43,530 --> 00:26:47,248
[nm]: And you want to be free from it, which is why you keep engaging with it.

458
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:47,920
[kc]: Yeah.

459
00:26:48,757 --> 00:26:50,754
[nm]: That's why sensuality pressures you.

460
00:26:51,190 --> 00:26:54,368
[nm]: Because it's underlined by the pain, simultaneously there.

461
00:26:54,900 --> 00:26:59,874
[nm]: And if you have any doubt about it, say no to yourself in regard to desire, and you'll see the pressure that builds up.

462
00:27:00,305 --> 00:27:01,105
[nm]: Why is that?

463
00:27:02,105 --> 00:27:03,400
[nm]: Why are you pressured?

464
00:27:04,108 --> 00:27:06,540
[nm]: Where is the... How is that pressure generated?

465
00:27:07,027 --> 00:27:08,408
[nm]: Pressure towards sense object.

466
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:18,142
[nm]: It's basically, directly corresponds, simultaneously, to the extent of craving that you maintain in regard to the pain that's being felt. Yeah.

467
00:27:18,597 --> 00:27:22,911
[nm]: You remove the craving in regard to the pain, there is no pressure towards the sense objects,

468
00:27:23,868 --> 00:27:29,091
[nm]: because the prospect of the pleasure of sense objects becomes non-applicable.

469
00:27:31,730 --> 00:27:44,531
[nm]: So, that's why it's important, like, I keep going back to this, I don't want to... like, we can talk about it later, about the danger and so on, escape, but it's all contained in first, then you can discern more within the first principle, and that's tha

470
00:27:45,122 --> 00:28:01,088
[nm]: Any degree of pleasure... so, imagine, actually, physical engagement with sensual pleasure... amidst of physical engagement with sensual pleasure, the pleasurability, pleasurability of physical engagement,

471
00:28:02,545 --> 00:28:08,271
[nm]: is actually the delighting in freedom from simultaneously enduring pain.

472
00:28:09,811 --> 00:28:11,745
[nm]: It's not coming from the senses.

473
00:28:12,540 --> 00:28:13,908
[nm]: It's coming from the pain.

474
00:28:15,454 --> 00:28:15,760
[nm]: So...

475
00:28:15,762 --> 00:28:17,163
[kc ]: The freedom from that pain, yeah.

476
00:28:17,228 --> 00:28:17,505
[nm]: Yeah.

477
00:28:17,500 --> 00:28:18,451
[nm]: Alleviation.

478
00:28:18,450 --> 00:28:19,048
[nm]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

479
00:28:19,585 --> 00:28:21,057
[nm]: To whatever extent.

480
00:28:21,862 --> 00:28:29,460
[nm]: So, again, it's important to imagine it on the right basis, which is sensuality, sensual engagement, sensual act...

481
00:28:30,610 --> 00:28:40,045
[nm]: pleasure of it, that you experience, that you used to experience, that you sometimes still might want to experience, doesn't matter the extent of it,

482
00:28:40,411 --> 00:28:44,094
[nm]: that pleasure is the alleviation of simultaneously enduring pain.

483
00:28:44,502 --> 00:28:47,145
[nm]: It's not the pleasure that comes to you through the senses.

484
00:28:50,182 --> 00:28:51,200
[nm]: It never leaves that.

485
00:28:51,617 --> 00:28:54,950
[nm]: You keep assuming pleasure to be external.

486
00:28:54,950 --> 00:28:55,290
[nm]: Hold on.

487
00:28:55,625 --> 00:28:57,951
[nm]: You keep assuming pleasure to be external...

488
00:28:59,074 --> 00:29:01,371
[nm]: to the presently enduring situation that is painful.

489
00:29:01,630 --> 00:29:02,725
[kc]: Which is the sensuality.

490
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:04,108
[nm]: Which is the assumption.

491
00:29:04,620 --> 00:29:04,890
[kc]: Yeah.

492
00:29:05,642 --> 00:29:06,310
[nm]: External?

493
00:29:06,310 --> 00:29:10,908
[nm]: How can you know... how can you know that this is pleasant while you're not engaging with it?

494
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:11,948
[kc]: So, the pleasure...

495
00:29:12,345 --> 00:29:13,331
[nm]: Again, imagine that.

496
00:29:13,554 --> 00:29:14,110
[kc]: Sorry, well...

497
00:29:14,110 --> 00:29:20,005
[nm]: There is a... there is a prospect of... of sensual, like, touch, of a pleasant nature, but you're not touching it.

498
00:29:20,320 --> 00:29:22,510
[nm]: Why is it felt pleasantly, that prospect?

499
00:29:22,610 --> 00:29:25,930
[nm]: Because you're... if... if the pleasure is in the object of your touch...

500
00:29:25,934 --> 00:29:26,548
[kc]: You're not even touching it.

501
00:29:26,540 --> 00:29:30,648
[nm]: How can you know that it's pleasant now, when you're not touching it?

502
00:29:30,700 --> 00:29:34,885
[nm]: Yet, and again, the argument of, oh, because you have a memory from before,

503
00:29:35,262 --> 00:29:36,860
[nm]: well, it still doesn't work;

504
00:29:37,300 --> 00:29:40,400
[nm]: because you are not elated on account of memory.

505
00:29:40,860 --> 00:29:44,702
[nm]: You're elated on account of the future prospect of, I'm about to touch this.

506
00:29:45,190 --> 00:29:48,348
[nm]: And yet, that's felt pleasantly before you touch it.

507
00:29:48,340 --> 00:29:48,810
[nm]: Why?

508
00:29:49,511 --> 00:29:54,530
[kc]: Because it provides the possibility of the alleviation of this pain.

509
00:29:54,530 --> 00:29:54,971
[nm]: No, because...

510
00:29:54,970 --> 00:29:56,062
[nm]: Well, yeah, okay, yeah.

511
00:29:56,060 --> 00:29:57,537
[nm]: Because the pain is there.

512
00:29:57,782 --> 00:29:58,991
[nm]: So, the pain is here,

513
00:30:00,057 --> 00:30:04,257
[nm]: claiming to get rid of this pain is here, which means prospect that I might be able to is here...

514
00:30:04,860 --> 00:30:10,900
[nm]: and then, whatever pleasure I feel in regard to anything out there, is because of this pain here.

515
00:30:10,900 --> 00:30:12,265
[kc]: And that pain is the pain of sensuality.

516
00:30:12,570 --> 00:30:12,797
[nm]: Yeah.

517
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,971
[nm]: And that pain is the pleasure of sensuality.

518
00:30:15,222 --> 00:30:15,511
[kc]: Yeah.

519
00:30:16,554 --> 00:30:18,350
[nm]: So then, when you go and engage with things...

520
00:30:18,350 --> 00:30:19,525
[kc]: The pleasure of sensuality...

521
00:30:19,520 --> 00:30:20,417
[nm]: is within that pain.

522
00:30:20,410 --> 00:30:21,077
[kc]: ...comes from that pain.

523
00:30:21,070 --> 00:30:22,165
[nm]: It doesn't come from it.

524
00:30:22,671 --> 00:30:23,657
[nm]: It stays within it.

525
00:30:23,960 --> 00:30:24,270
[kc]: Okay.

526
00:30:24,270 --> 00:30:25,717
[nm]: That's the important... That's what I'm trying to...

527
00:30:25,710 --> 00:30:26,130
[kc]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

528
00:30:26,130 --> 00:30:27,077
[nm]: to hammer in here.

529
00:30:28,045 --> 00:30:34,308
[nm]: Because, basically, hammer that in, and there is no basis for assuming external to this experience of sensuality.

530
00:30:34,837 --> 00:30:39,985
[nm]: And you do assume the sense objects to be external to your experience of desire.

531
00:30:40,570 --> 00:30:47,460
[nm]: Which is why it's insatiable, because you perverted the order, and this domain of sense object it's completely not applicable.

532
00:30:47,514 --> 00:30:55,748
[nm]: As I said, you're not even engaging with it, yet you are feeling pleasure on account of the prospect of engaging with, on the level of the senses.

533
00:30:56,120 --> 00:31:00,545
[nm]: There is a desire there, and that desire is felt like you're delighting in it.

534
00:31:00,868 --> 00:31:01,420
[nm]: Why?

535
00:31:01,774 --> 00:31:07,382
[nm]: Because that desire is fully within this pain, that's simultaneously enduring to the same extent.

536
00:31:08,740 --> 00:31:21,777
[nm]: So, if you stop assuming that then the pleasure of alleviating the pain through following that desire is contained external to the pain and the desire, you will stop perverting the order.

537
00:31:23,877 --> 00:31:28,351
[nm]: In the same sense, you stop assuming your sense of self to be outside of your experience as a whole.

538
00:31:28,350 --> 00:31:29,834
[nm]: You realize that's inconceivable.

539
00:31:34,231 --> 00:31:36,022
[nm]: Same principle of the same upādāna.

540
00:31:36,020 --> 00:31:36,220
[kc]: Hang on.

541
00:31:36,220 --> 00:31:41,760
[kc]: So, seeing the pleasure as being external to the pain, is basically seeing...

542
00:31:41,760 --> 00:31:42,300
[nm]: Okay, there you go.

543
00:31:42,300 --> 00:31:43,191
[nm]: You already said it.

544
00:31:43,688 --> 00:31:46,325
[nm]: A thought of pleasure might be external to the pain.

545
00:31:47,468 --> 00:31:48,148
[nm]: How would you know that?

546
00:31:48,414 --> 00:31:51,268
[nm]: Without engaging with that where the pleasure might be, which you are not.

547
00:31:52,342 --> 00:31:54,417
[nm]: It doesn't matter the extent of your thought.

548
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:59,728
[nm]: As I said before, like when you say, okay, I think I'm outside of this experience as a whole.

549
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:01,668
[nm]: Okay, so I'm not outside of this experience as a whole.

550
00:32:01,660 --> 00:32:02,977
[nm]: Something else is.

551
00:32:03,282 --> 00:32:06,557
[nm]: But then, that can only be the thought that's within this experience as a whole.

552
00:32:07,331 --> 00:32:09,000
[nm]: Yeah, but then there's the outside of that thought.

553
00:32:09,388 --> 00:32:10,880
[nm]: Which can only be within...

554
00:32:11,022 --> 00:32:14,882
[nm]: It's the same principle in this case, once you start from the right level.

555
00:32:15,282 --> 00:32:22,082
[nm]: So, the pleasure that's outside of this desire that has arisen, is within this desire that has arisen.

556
00:32:22,500 --> 00:32:27,494
[nm]: Because how can then you feel it pleasantly, that prospect of that pleasure, unless it's within this desire?

557
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:32,374
[nm]: And that's pretty much all you need to clarify,

558
00:32:32,750 --> 00:32:40,654
[nm]: but all the way, and it will become... well, you will become unable to think that pleasure is in sense objects.

559
00:32:40,874 --> 00:32:44,540
[nm]: That beautiful objects in the world are the ones that have pleasure in them.

560
00:32:45,517 --> 00:32:47,237
[nm]: And that's how sensuality falls off.

561
00:32:48,380 --> 00:32:54,017
[nm]: Doesn't mean you... you wouldn't recognize nice food or agreeable touch, but you certainly wouldn't crave for it.

562
00:32:54,605 --> 00:32:54,977
[nm]: Why?

563
00:32:54,970 --> 00:32:57,985
[nm]: Because you don't crave for gratuitous freedom from unpleasantness.

564
00:32:59,610 --> 00:33:00,260
[kc]: Because...

565
00:33:00,382 --> 00:33:04,080
[nm]: You don't crave to alleviate by default of anything that's felt discomfortably.

566
00:33:04,080 --> 00:33:08,150
[kc]: That's because that pleasure cannot possibly undo that more fundamental pain.

567
00:33:08,150 --> 00:33:09,434
[nm]: No. It's always... exactly.

568
00:33:09,430 --> 00:33:11,037
[nm]: It's always within that.

569
00:33:11,208 --> 00:33:11,890
[kc]: So, that's the thing.

570
00:33:11,890 --> 00:33:18,660
[kc]: So, you're basically trying to get rid of something by expecting something more particular to get under its roots.

571
00:33:18,660 --> 00:33:19,122
[nm]: Sure.

572
00:33:19,342 --> 00:33:19,728
[nm]: Sure.

573
00:33:19,990 --> 00:33:27,651
[kc]: Whereas, actually, you... that pain is there whether you like it or not and... you...

574
00:33:27,960 --> 00:33:33,462
[nm]: And again, ironically, you want to be free from it, which is why you engage with sensuality.

575
00:33:33,925 --> 00:33:38,314
[nm]: So, all you need to do is recognize that it's painful first, and you want to be free from it.

576
00:33:38,890 --> 00:33:41,900
[nm]: Thus, the best course of action, then, is to not engage with it.

577
00:33:43,254 --> 00:33:53,285
[nm]: But then, that means you now have to be able to endure for as long as it takes, not acting out of the gratuitous assumption of craving in regard to the unpleasant enduring feeling.

578
00:33:55,471 --> 00:34:05,417
[nm]: But then, even when you have a thought, a memory of previous sensuality, a thought of the future sensuality, and it's... and the mind delights in it, you don't deny that.

579
00:34:05,811 --> 00:34:08,474
[nm]: You just see it as included within this pain.

580
00:34:09,202 --> 00:34:19,860
[nm]: And that the pleasure that's felt, even if you were to engage, even when you eat the food that's agreeable, the pleasure you're feeling is the alleviation of the simultaneous enduring pain.

581
00:34:19,860 --> 00:34:20,091
[kc]: Yeah.

582
00:34:20,368 --> 00:34:21,668
[kc]: It's putting pain first.

583
00:34:22,340 --> 00:34:22,611
[nm]: Yeah.

584
00:34:23,188 --> 00:34:23,671
[kc]: Basically...

585
00:34:23,671 --> 00:34:25,570
[nm]: Or not allowing it to be assumed second.
[kc]: Basically...

586
00:34:25,570 --> 00:34:25,597
[nm]: Or not allowing it to be assumed second.

587
00:34:25,770 --> 00:34:26,070
[kc]: Yeah.

588
00:34:26,380 --> 00:34:28,765
[kc]: So, not allowing it to be assumed second. So, not...

589
00:34:28,760 --> 00:34:32,185
[nm]: And it gets assumed second when you... when you become careless.

590
00:34:32,562 --> 00:34:34,530
[kc]: When you're basically not mindful of the feeling.

591
00:34:34,530 --> 00:34:34,805
[nm]: Yeah.

592
00:34:34,800 --> 00:34:36,328
[kc]: At the general most... at the general level.

593
00:34:36,617 --> 00:34:38,097
[nm]: Or when you lose sense restrain.

594
00:34:42,640 --> 00:34:54,551
[b0]: Like that... the past or the future... a future prospect or the past experience, that's already, like...

595
00:34:55,465 --> 00:34:58,100
[b0]: That's pain right here right now, isn't it? Like...

596
00:34:58,100 --> 00:34:58,788
[nm]: Exactly.

597
00:34:59,068 --> 00:34:59,831
[nm]: Yeah, yeah.

598
00:34:59,891 --> 00:35:01,117
[nm]: That's another thing, yeah.

599
00:35:01,110 --> 00:35:02,122
[nm]: You can clarify.

600
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:09,791
[nm]: So, how would you know that the past prospects were pleasant, unless you're feeling them now pleasurably?

601
00:35:12,148 --> 00:35:19,937
[nm]: How would you know that the future prospect of engaging with a particular sense object... Oh, why are you feeling it pleasurably right here, right now?

602
00:35:20,685 --> 00:35:29,797
[nm]: So, the extent, doesn't matter the extent, how particular, how committed to a particular aspect of a sense object that you're deriving pleasure from.

603
00:35:30,211 --> 00:35:35,834
[nm]: Any pleasure derived from any sense action is the pleasure of alleviating simultaneously enduring pain.

604
00:35:36,302 --> 00:35:38,614
[nm]: It's not the pleasure that comes from the object.

605
00:35:39,665 --> 00:35:50,620
[nm]: And the reason why you have pressure to engage with the object, is because that's how you give validity to the direction of engagement, which is what alleviates the pain, not gets you the pleasure from the sense object.

606
00:35:50,620 --> 00:35:52,357
[nm]: There is no pleasure in the sense objects.

607
00:35:52,350 --> 00:35:56,368
[nm]: It's just objects of perceptions, which are neither pleasurable nor displeasurable.

608
00:35:57,774 --> 00:36:03,390
[nm]: Yet, you're feeling pleasurable on account of... and as well, that's why people like to pursue sensual object.

609
00:36:03,390 --> 00:36:05,111
[nm]: If it's just given, eh...

610
00:36:06,220 --> 00:36:10,402
[nm]: But if it's a bit taken away, taken away, taken away, your pleasure grows.

611
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:13,110
[nm]: Why would that happen, if the pleasure were truly in the object?

612
00:36:13,110 --> 00:36:14,437
[nm]: Because you haven't touched it yet.

613
00:36:14,477 --> 00:36:16,097
[nm]: How do you know that there's more of it?

614
00:36:16,090 --> 00:36:18,140
[nm]: Yet, there is more of it in your mind.

615
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:33,380
[nm]: So, the desire grows, because the engagement towards that direction grows, because you chose to basically go that way, which means that the... the extent of the prospect of alleviating this also presently enduring pain, grows.

616
00:36:35,205 --> 00:36:41,565
[nm]: So, the pressure grows, because you, yourself, made it so.

617
00:36:42,170 --> 00:36:58,874
[kc]: The way the Buddha describes the five strands of sensuality, he says, it's like sights that you can be conscious of with the eye, but you can be conscious of, you could be conscious of, cakkhuviññeyya...

618
00:37:00,514 --> 00:37:03,662
[kc]: So, it's like, it's specific there, saying, basically, you are...

619
00:37:04,707 --> 00:37:06,568
[kc]: that the sensuality is the possibility.

620
00:37:08,228 --> 00:37:08,494
[kc]: Where is it?

621
00:37:08,490 --> 00:37:10,700
[kc]: Cakkhuviññeyya, in the Pali.

622
00:37:10,700 --> 00:37:16,225
[kc]: So, it's sights cogniz... Bhikkhu Bodhi translates it as sights cognizable, by the...

623
00:37:16,350 --> 00:37:17,677
[nm]: Cognizable.

624
00:37:17,754 --> 00:37:18,550
[nm]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

625
00:37:18,550 --> 00:37:20,834
[kc]: Viññeyya, which means it could be...

626
00:37:20,865 --> 00:37:21,477
[nm]: Sure, sure.

627
00:37:21,470 --> 00:37:22,134
[kc]: cognized.

628
00:37:22,354 --> 00:37:23,070
[kc]: Not that it is.

629
00:37:23,070 --> 00:37:24,997
[kc]: No, it's all on the level of possibility.

630
00:37:25,020 --> 00:37:25,437
[nm]: Yeah.

631
00:37:26,028 --> 00:37:26,530
[nm]: It is.

632
00:37:26,530 --> 00:37:26,822
[kc]: Yeah.

633
00:37:27,840 --> 00:37:30,397
[nm]: Because it already starts there, as soon as you're subjected to pain.

634
00:37:30,914 --> 00:37:35,891
[nm]: And that's why also the Buddha said, the only way that Putujana knows out of pain, is through sensuality.

635
00:37:37,030 --> 00:37:44,280
[nm]: Which is not out of pain, but it's the only way he knows that they would closely resemble to dealing with pain.

636
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:45,430
[kc]: It's what he thinks will...

637
00:37:45,430 --> 00:37:47,945
[nm]: Well, no. There is a degree of alleviation.

638
00:37:48,842 --> 00:37:51,182
[nm]: If it weren't so, you wouldn't be pressured by it either.

639
00:37:52,474 --> 00:38:06,237
[nm]: But it's that pursuit, that delight in the possibility of that direction, engaging with it, kind of magically gives the validity of: oh, yes, because I'm doing this, that's why I'm not subjected to this... which you are, obviously, still subjected to.

640
00:38:06,230 --> 00:38:12,131
[nm]: Otherwise, you wouldn't be going down the pursuit, if you're not subjected to the unpleasant desire of it beforehand.

641
00:38:12,340 --> 00:38:13,531
[kc]: So, that's the gratification.

642
00:38:13,702 --> 00:38:13,951
[nm]: Yeah.

643
00:38:13,977 --> 00:38:18,870
[kc]: Seeing the gratification is just seeing that any pleasure you could possibly have now is still within.

644
00:38:18,870 --> 00:38:22,031
[nm]: And that's why, as the Buddha said, gratification is on the level of the delight.

645
00:38:22,788 --> 00:38:24,297
[nm]: You're delighting in the prospect.

646
00:38:26,328 --> 00:38:32,940
[b0]: So, you have... when you have, like, something secured, you extend, sort of, like, consuming it.

647
00:38:32,940 --> 00:38:34,045
[nm]: Sure, sure, sure.

648
00:38:34,074 --> 00:38:34,408
[nm]: Yeah.

649
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:35,122
[nm]: You prolong it.

650
00:38:35,591 --> 00:38:35,848
[kc]: Yeah.

651
00:38:37,250 --> 00:38:42,622
[nm]: Because if you just do it, oh, it becomes obvious how it cannot possibly pertain to the domain you're acting from.

652
00:38:54,828 --> 00:39:06,891
[nm]: So, the extent of your sensual cravings is directly determined by the extent of your craving against the painful feeling that you're subjected to.

653
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:09,490
[kc]: That's all it is... to see...

654
00:39:09,490 --> 00:39:19,368
[nm]: So, any... like when you... and again, as I said, you always start with a... like the... the order you have to start with is the order that's affected with ignorance.

655
00:39:19,810 --> 00:39:21,288
[nm]: You can't start things rightly.

656
00:39:21,765 --> 00:39:24,870
[nm]: So, now, okay, yeah, delighting is, in sensuality, is a problem.

657
00:39:24,870 --> 00:39:26,330
[nm]: But, oh, I must stop delighting.

658
00:39:26,330 --> 00:39:27,905
[nm]: Well, it's not quite a method of choice.

659
00:39:28,300 --> 00:39:30,797
[nm]: Delighting is a symptom of an underlying assumption.

660
00:39:31,460 --> 00:39:43,831
[nm]: So, in that case, when you are delighting in the prospect of sensuality, you want to then make sure you include the delight and the prospect of sensual pursuit that you're restraining against, but the prospect is still there.

661
00:39:43,830 --> 00:39:52,288
[nm]: So, you want to include the whole thing, including the future sense object, within the container of pain that's presently enduring.

662
00:39:53,208 --> 00:39:57,297
[nm]: Not left, not right, not before, and certainly not after it.

663
00:39:58,288 --> 00:40:01,194
[nm]: Because that whole assumption that, eh...

664
00:40:01,330 --> 00:40:05,954
[nm]: I have a desire, then I engage and I set, like, satisfy the desire. Desire runs away.

665
00:40:06,582 --> 00:40:06,942
[nm]: No.

666
00:40:08,508 --> 00:40:13,562
[nm]: It's just you... you get tired, basically, from running away from the pain, that then you accept it.

667
00:40:14,622 --> 00:40:15,634
[nm]: And it ceases to hurt.

668
00:40:16,994 --> 00:40:19,080
[nm]: So, what if you were to accept the pain right away?

669
00:40:19,885 --> 00:40:24,671
[nm]: And removing the middleman of central pursuits that cannot possibly even pertain to the domain of pain.

670
00:40:25,240 --> 00:40:28,685
[nm]: Then, you realize you'll be above the pain even before the pain.

671
00:40:32,988 --> 00:40:34,720
[nm]: You can't satisfy your desires.

672
00:40:35,442 --> 00:40:45,925
[nm]: But nobody denies that after a degree of engagement with your sensuality, projected goals of your desires, you don't feel painful anymore.

673
00:40:46,248 --> 00:40:46,928
[nm]: Why is that?

674
00:40:49,991 --> 00:40:52,382
[nm]: So, the sense object remains unchanged.

675
00:40:52,862 --> 00:40:56,197
[nm]: In a way, like you haven't truly consumed it and destroyed it.

676
00:40:56,505 --> 00:40:58,128
[nm]: It's still there, things you've been touching.

677
00:40:58,254 --> 00:41:01,842
[nm]: Even the food, in a way, it's still there, just now in the stomach, as opposed to the table,

678
00:41:02,377 --> 00:41:10,028
[nm]: so, nothing has come out of the material domain, into you, or got consumed by the all-powerful sense of self.

679
00:41:10,820 --> 00:41:12,022
[nm]: Yet, there is no pain now.

680
00:41:12,380 --> 00:41:12,880
[nm]: Why is that?

681
00:41:12,882 --> 00:41:14,022
[kc]: Well, you just covered it over.

682
00:41:14,714 --> 00:41:15,954
[nm]: How? How can you cover it over?

683
00:41:16,840 --> 00:41:19,702
[kc]: By... by...

684
00:41:20,477 --> 00:41:24,268
[nm]: How can you cover the door when the domain of senses cannot possibly pertain to the domain of feelings?

685
00:41:25,811 --> 00:41:26,270
[kc]: Okay.

686
00:41:26,270 --> 00:41:27,000
[nm]: What has changed?

687
00:41:30,580 --> 00:41:31,988
[b0]: So, you stop perceiving.

688
00:41:33,068 --> 00:41:34,908
[nm]: No, you're not perceiving the pain anyway,

689
00:41:35,080 --> 00:41:35,780
[nm]: You're feeling it.

690
00:41:36,208 --> 00:41:36,965
[nm]: What has changed?

691
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,037
[nm]: Pursuing it...

692
00:41:38,737 --> 00:41:41,302
[nm]: Yeah, but you stop pursuing it because it doesn't hurt anymore.

693
00:41:41,714 --> 00:41:42,702
[nm]: The pressure is gone.

694
00:41:42,857 --> 00:41:43,611
[nm]: Why is that?

695
00:41:44,885 --> 00:41:46,410
[nm]: Why is it that it doesn't hurt anymore?

696
00:41:46,410 --> 00:41:47,774
[nm]: Why did it hurt in the first place?

697
00:41:48,771 --> 00:41:50,768
[kc]: Because you were just subjected to a painful feeling.

698
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:52,357
[nm]: No, that's not suffering.

699
00:41:53,025 --> 00:41:54,400
[nm]: Painful feeling is not dukkha.

700
00:41:55,850 --> 00:41:58,494
[nm]: Craving to be free from painful feeling is what dukkha is.

701
00:41:58,951 --> 00:42:00,668
[nm]: So that's the only thing that changed.

702
00:42:01,054 --> 00:42:09,882
[nm]: After a certain amount of engagement with sensual object, pursuit of it in particular, you stopped resisting the unpleasant feeling in itself.

703
00:42:11,505 --> 00:42:12,614
[nm]: And that's why you don't suffer.

704
00:42:16,854 --> 00:42:20,142
[nm]: But pursuit of sensual object had nothing to do with you stop resisting it.

705
00:42:20,510 --> 00:42:31,614
[nm]: It was basically the aversion. And that's why, exactly, sometimes, if you keep engaging with the pursuit of the sense-objects, it becomes apparent that you cannot do anything to the pain you're feeling.

706
00:42:32,128 --> 00:42:33,008
[nm]: So, what you do then?

707
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:33,860
[nm]: You double down.

708
00:42:33,970 --> 00:42:34,754
[nm]: You triple down.

709
00:42:36,082 --> 00:42:39,517
[nm]: And that's how perception of sense-objects proliferates.

710
00:42:39,645 --> 00:42:42,617
[nm]: Because it has nothing to do with the domain that you're actually acting from.

711
00:42:44,497 --> 00:42:46,331
[nm]: And then, yeah, you go to the extremes.

712
00:42:48,448 --> 00:42:56,914
[nm]: Just to... hoping that some of it will allow your mind to take it as a successful project of diversion, basically.

713
00:42:57,700 --> 00:43:00,234
[nm]: So, you don't know how to stop craving the feeling.

714
00:43:00,580 --> 00:43:08,108
[nm]: You're just doing these random things, hoping that it will result in you, at least temporarily, forgetting about resisting the pain.

715
00:43:09,677 --> 00:43:13,440
[nm]: And that's why you have to stop engaging with sensuality first.

716
00:43:13,560 --> 00:43:17,520
[nm]: Even if you're completely ignorant, you have to start practicing sense restraint first.

717
00:43:20,570 --> 00:43:27,285
[nm]: Because it's basically, it's on the level of a magical belief, a diversion that you know deep down has nothing... and everybody knows that.

718
00:43:27,774 --> 00:43:30,430
[nm]: I was saying that to Venerable Ṭhāniyo a while ago.

719
00:43:30,910 --> 00:43:40,265
[nm]: Like, I remember even way before, like, when I was in my teens, before I started reading the Buddhism itself, you always knew deep down you can't satisfy your desires.

720
00:43:40,485 --> 00:43:48,665
[nm]: Talking with friends about it, like, you can't satisfy... yeah, you can't help but pursuing them, but you know already you can't satisfy them.

721
00:43:49,340 --> 00:43:57,314
[nm]: So, the only thing that changes, like, before the pursuit and after pursuit, is your own attitude in regard to what you're already feeling, what you've been feeling all along.

722
00:43:57,840 --> 00:43:58,360
[nm]: That's it.

723
00:43:59,311 --> 00:44:10,440
[nm]: So, you use sense engagement to tire yourself out, so you can't crave the resistance, you can't maintain the resistance towards unpleasantly enduring feeling, and it ceases to be unpleasant.

724
00:44:12,174 --> 00:44:13,170
[kc]: Yeah, that's what I was going to say.

725
00:44:13,170 --> 00:44:14,668
[kc]: It's not unpleasant, if you don't...

726
00:44:14,940 --> 00:44:15,790
[kc]: It's not unpleasant.

727
00:44:15,790 --> 00:44:16,940
[nm]: It's not suffering, yeah.

728
00:44:17,442 --> 00:44:21,794
[nm]: But habitually, anything disagreeable is resisted, and you make it into suffering.

729
00:44:26,022 --> 00:44:40,325
[nm]: And yeah, many times, and I'm sure everybody experienced that, at some point, even after the culmination of your sensual satisfaction of objects, the mind is still completely unsatisfied, and you want more.

730
00:44:40,451 --> 00:44:41,820
[nm]: The body can't have more.

731
00:44:43,300 --> 00:44:54,834
[nm]: The body's fatigue doesn't... the ich has been scratched so much, it hurts, yet, the mental attitude of having their desire completely unchanged, and you're just going mad, basically, with the desire,

732
00:44:55,180 --> 00:45:03,942
[nm]: because you've been giving in to that domain of sense pursuit that had nothing to do with this, and that's the only way you know.

733
00:45:04,548 --> 00:45:10,140
[kc]: Yeah, so are you saying that when you've kind of...

734
00:45:10,742 --> 00:45:16,022
[kc]: gone for, sort of, gratifying your desires and then afterwards you feel, sort of, you feel satisfied...

735
00:45:17,282 --> 00:45:25,245
[kc]: That's because, that's basically because, through your acts, you've actually reduced craving.

736
00:45:27,220 --> 00:45:28,217
[kc]: Because there's no suffering.

737
00:45:30,148 --> 00:45:32,570
[nm]: Eh... Well, I won't say you reduced it.

738
00:45:32,570 --> 00:45:33,850
[kc]: Yeah, exactly. Do you know what I mean?

739
00:45:33,850 --> 00:45:34,948
[kc]: Like, temporarily...

740
00:45:34,940 --> 00:45:36,105
[nm]: Well, you stop doing it.

741
00:45:36,100 --> 00:45:37,991
[kc]: Not the possibility of craving, obviously.

742
00:45:37,990 --> 00:45:38,860
[nm]: Sure, sure, sure.

743
00:45:38,860 --> 00:45:40,094
[nm]: Oh, yeah, no, that's true, yeah.

744
00:45:40,465 --> 00:45:42,240
[nm]: Resistance to suffering is craving.

745
00:45:42,240 --> 00:45:42,522
[kc]: Yeah.

746
00:45:42,665 --> 00:45:44,637
[nm]: You stop resisting when you tire yourself out.

747
00:45:44,774 --> 00:45:47,537
[kc]: So, actually, by scratching, I am actually reducing...

748
00:45:47,530 --> 00:45:48,500
[nm]: You are, you are.

749
00:45:48,500 --> 00:45:50,274
[nm]: No, that's why it is gratification.

750
00:45:50,270 --> 00:45:51,130
[nm]: That's how I started this.

751
00:45:51,134 --> 00:45:51,720
[kc]: That's why you're doing it.

752
00:45:51,720 --> 00:45:57,620
[nm]: That's why the Buddha, like, if there is no gratification, you wouldn't have called it. It does, it does gratify something...

753
00:45:58,617 --> 00:46:04,977
[nm]: and you realize, even the gratification has nothing to do with sense objects, has to do with your own attitude towards your own craving.

754
00:46:05,560 --> 00:46:08,440
[nm]: Towards your own feeling, sorry, which is already an attitude of craving.

755
00:46:09,485 --> 00:46:30,365
[nm]: So, yes, through scratching your itch, you are reducing craving, but simultaneously making your dependence on running away of pain even harder, even stronger, which means, oh, so through reducing this craving, actually, I am fueling more, like, I'll be more subjected to even more craving later on.

756
00:46:30,840 --> 00:46:34,211
[tn]: Because I need that desire to keep on scratching.

757
00:46:34,397 --> 00:46:35,420
[nm]: Yeah. Exactly.

758
00:46:35,420 --> 00:46:36,900
[tn]: So, it just fuels itself.

759
00:46:36,900 --> 00:46:37,751
[kc]: Because that's the only...

760
00:46:37,750 --> 00:46:38,940
[nm]: That's what I mean.

761
00:46:38,940 --> 00:46:49,185
[nm]: That's why first you have to stop doing it, and then you realize that even the acts of doing it were rooted in actuall:, oh, it's simply because I don't want this pain, as in I gratuitously resist it.

762
00:46:49,960 --> 00:46:52,288
[nm]: But it's not painful if I don't resist it.

763
00:46:52,980 --> 00:46:55,300
[nm]: It's painful if I resist it and then interfere with it.

764
00:46:55,300 --> 00:46:58,445
[nm]: Means, okay, I gave it validity, next time I'll resist it even more.

765
00:46:59,048 --> 00:47:05,660
[nm]: So, what if I... okay, now I stopped engaging with it, stopped maintaining these wrong avenues of trying to deal with it, stopped scratching my itch...

766
00:47:06,411 --> 00:47:10,842
[nm]: What if I now to endure the pain, not act out of it, and then just stop resisting it?

767
00:47:10,840 --> 00:47:12,068
[nm]: Not try to get rid of it.

768
00:47:12,390 --> 00:47:13,128
[nm]: That's another thing.

769
00:47:13,390 --> 00:47:13,550
[kc]: Yeah.

770
00:47:13,550 --> 00:47:14,431
[nm]: Because if people, I must...

771
00:47:14,430 --> 00:47:16,300
[kc]: I must, I'll resist it and then it'll go away.

772
00:47:16,300 --> 00:47:16,862
[nm]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

773
00:47:16,860 --> 00:47:17,765
[nm]: Or like asubha.

774
00:47:17,760 --> 00:47:21,700
[nm]: Asubha becomes for people getting rid of the sensual pain.

775
00:47:21,734 --> 00:47:24,702
[tn]: Because, yeah, I must resist it so it doesn't bother me.

776
00:47:24,700 --> 00:47:25,142
[nm]: Exactly.

777
00:47:25,140 --> 00:47:25,405
[kc]: Yeah.

778
00:47:25,537 --> 00:47:28,665
[nm]: So, the pain is there if it has... if sensuality has arisen.

779
00:47:28,742 --> 00:47:31,314
[nm]: That's why sensuality in its nature is harassing.

780
00:47:31,810 --> 00:47:33,730
[nm]: That is the nature of sense objects.

781
00:47:33,730 --> 00:47:34,522
[nm]: They harass you.

782
00:47:34,868 --> 00:47:35,362
[nm]: No, no, no.

783
00:47:35,362 --> 00:47:35,654
[kc]: I was saying...

784
00:47:35,650 --> 00:47:36,797
[nm]: Even before your craving.

785
00:47:36,790 --> 00:47:37,500
[lc]: Oh, I see.

786
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:37,870
[kc]: I see.

787
00:47:37,870 --> 00:47:38,790
[kc]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

788
00:47:38,790 --> 00:47:49,957
[nm]: The significance, the implications of a female body for a man, or male body for a woman, or food for a hungry person, the implications are forceful.

789
00:47:51,134 --> 00:47:52,894
[nm]: Even... no effort required.

790
00:47:53,454 --> 00:47:55,614
[nm]: Forceful is felt unpleasantly.

791
00:47:56,602 --> 00:48:03,117
[nm]: And then, automatically, simultaneously, unenlightened mind resists any form of unpleasure.

792
00:48:03,900 --> 00:48:15,528
[nm]: So, you experience forceful perceptions, automatically, you're already resisting them, which means, automatically, you're already delighting in them, to get the freedom from this resistance, that you're responsible for.

793
00:48:15,840 --> 00:48:18,977
[nm]: That's why in Arahant, eh... Anuruddha,

794
00:48:20,488 --> 00:48:26,994
[nm]: When he was... when that woman took him, oh, you can stay in this room, and then came there and took her clothes off, and tried to basically sleep with him.

795
00:48:27,771 --> 00:48:39,174
[nm]: And the sutta says that he just sat cross-legged and was kind of... became mindful of his breathing, and she was sort of dancing, trying to get his attention, then felt embarrassed, because he wasn't... and then dressed up and apologized.

796
00:48:40,111 --> 00:48:43,951
[nm]: I remember the first time I read the sutta, I thought, well, why would Arahant even need to be mindful of his breath?

797
00:48:44,830 --> 00:48:47,205
[nm]: Why would he... like, I thought Arahant would be just completely...

798
00:48:48,880 --> 00:48:49,480
[nm]: blind.

799
00:48:50,420 --> 00:48:52,362
[nm]: But, no, he was aware of the significance.

800
00:48:52,494 --> 00:48:54,445
[nm]: And that significance is actually harassing.

801
00:48:55,120 --> 00:48:55,945
[nm]: It's unpleasant.

802
00:48:56,517 --> 00:49:00,717
[nm]: So, he was mindful of his breath, just because he was subjected to pain.

803
00:49:01,948 --> 00:49:03,571
[nm]: Not because he tried to get rid of it.

804
00:49:04,597 --> 00:49:11,897
[nm]: So, okay, well, this harassment now, until it stops, I'll just sort of be mindful of my experience as a whole, while I'm being tortured.

805
00:49:12,670 --> 00:49:27,180
[nm]: That's why Raṭṭhapālasutta, when he goes home, already anāgāmī, maybe even an arahant, and the father tells all his wives to dress up provocatively how they used to, how he used to like it, and they go and start trying to seduce him, he says, stop harassing me.

806
00:49:27,180 --> 00:49:28,008
[nm]: This is harassing.

807
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:31,151
[nm]: Like... And it is.

808
00:49:31,662 --> 00:49:33,040
[nm]: And that's the nature of the senses.

809
00:49:33,040 --> 00:49:39,445
[nm]: So, you are harassed by your senses being subjected to these forceful sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches.

810
00:49:40,482 --> 00:49:41,314
[nm]: Again, like a dog.

811
00:49:41,960 --> 00:49:43,557
[nm]: He hears something. He can't help it.

812
00:49:43,740 --> 00:49:46,200
[nm]: He can't help it, but he wants to go there now.

813
00:49:46,620 --> 00:49:49,497
[nm]: But you don't need to resist that experience as a whole.

814
00:49:49,650 --> 00:49:54,508
[kc]: That level of harassment, doesn't that apply to any at all?

815
00:49:54,500 --> 00:49:55,071
[nm]: It does.

816
00:49:55,070 --> 00:49:57,962
[nm]: Fundamentally, so, basically, whether it's painful or pleasant...

817
00:49:57,960 --> 00:50:03,420
[nm]: That's why, if you were to undo the craving on the absolute fundamental level, sensuality would be undone as well.

818
00:50:03,420 --> 00:50:03,562
[kc]: Yeah.

819
00:50:03,560 --> 00:50:04,780
[nm]: It cannot possibly remain.

820
00:50:05,485 --> 00:50:08,782
[nm]: But, more practically, you might have to address it in itself.

821
00:50:10,840 --> 00:50:16,765
[b0]: Let's go back to that. Neglecting the painful feeling...

822
00:50:16,842 --> 00:50:17,228
[nm]: Yeah.

823
00:50:17,220 --> 00:50:17,931
[b0]: that's...

824
00:50:17,930 --> 00:50:21,325
[nm]: Everything goes... that's the only... that's why I keep saying... The suttas say that.

825
00:50:21,534 --> 00:50:23,340
[nm]: Things converge in feelings.

826
00:50:23,397 --> 00:50:24,222
[nm]: Always.

827
00:50:24,494 --> 00:50:26,568
[nm]: Not sometimes, not every other day.

828
00:50:26,854 --> 00:50:27,660
[nm]: Always.

829
00:50:28,200 --> 00:50:31,865
[nm]: Which means your action, your motivation, your perceptions, basically, your moods.

830
00:50:32,648 --> 00:50:33,668
[nm]: Where do they converge?

831
00:50:33,660 --> 00:50:35,680
[nm]: Converge on how you're feeling right here, right now.

832
00:50:35,680 --> 00:50:37,177
[nm]: And that feeling endures.

833
00:50:37,525 --> 00:50:38,240
[nm]: So, here you are.

834
00:50:38,240 --> 00:50:40,145
[nm]: Can't stop thinking about a central object.

835
00:50:40,200 --> 00:50:41,257
[nm]: Where does it converge?

836
00:50:41,374 --> 00:50:44,980
[nm]: Converge on presently enduring feeling of discomfort that you're resisting.

837
00:50:45,617 --> 00:50:50,620
[nm]: You want to get rid of it, but not by any... by means of distracting yourself in this direction.

838
00:50:50,758 --> 00:50:51,118
[nm]: That's it.

839
00:50:52,188 --> 00:51:02,954
[nm]: And again, imagine... well, imagine being really, really hungry, and you eat something not even so tasty, but it provides you this great pleasure.

840
00:51:03,597 --> 00:51:10,985
[nm]: And then, imagine you're full to the point of feeling sick, and somebody brings something extremely tasty, and you're still sick.

841
00:51:12,610 --> 00:51:13,925
[nm]: There is no pleasure in eating it.

842
00:51:14,717 --> 00:51:20,091
[nm]: Again, if the pleasure were in these sense objects, that wouldn't be the case.

843
00:51:20,571 --> 00:51:23,291
[nm]: Every time you were to eat a pleasant thing, it would be felt pleasantly.

844
00:51:24,170 --> 00:51:27,022
[nm]: But when you're hungry, things that were not pleasant, feel pleasantly,

845
00:51:27,820 --> 00:51:30,971
[nm]: and when you're not hungry, things that are pleasant, feel unpleasantly.

846
00:51:33,368 --> 00:51:34,654
[nm]: So, what's in common to that?

847
00:51:34,650 --> 00:51:38,891
[nm]: Well, it's in common to that whatever your senses are subjected to, is in a way forceful.

848
00:51:41,428 --> 00:51:42,782
[nm]: Agreeable or disagreeable.

849
00:51:42,780 --> 00:51:43,460
[nm]: It pushes you.

850
00:51:43,460 --> 00:51:46,291
[nm]: Significance implies, requires you, pressures you.

851
00:51:46,631 --> 00:51:48,700
[nm]: But, all of that will work,

852
00:51:48,700 --> 00:51:55,140
[nm]: that whole domain of being pressured, implied, pulled, forced upon, will work only if you provide a basis for it,

853
00:51:55,140 --> 00:51:57,040
[nm]: and the basis is, I resist the discomfort.

854
00:51:59,840 --> 00:52:04,331
[nm]: And that's that's how you then become pulled and forced and oppressed.

855
00:52:05,437 --> 00:52:14,831
[nm]: You stop resisting the comfort, none of these things, discomfort, none of these things can possibly enter you, or certainly exercise any influence over you.

856
00:52:16,457 --> 00:52:23,980
[tn]: So the assumption, we have assumption is, there's a prospect of pleasure and...

857
00:52:25,960 --> 00:52:31,231
[tn]: I can get that, but you're not recognizing the pain where it's coming from.

858
00:52:31,230 --> 00:52:37,680
[nm]: Yeah. More precisely, assumption is, assuming the pleasure to be external to the pain, that's it.

859
00:52:38,811 --> 00:52:39,740
[kc]: External.

860
00:52:40,020 --> 00:52:40,531
[nm]: That's it.

861
00:52:40,897 --> 00:52:41,690
[kc]: External to it.

862
00:52:41,690 --> 00:52:41,760
[nm]: So, assuming pleasure to be external to the present enduring pain, that's the assumption of sensuality, isn't it?
[kc]: External to it.

863
00:52:41,760 --> 00:52:48,285
[nm]: So, assuming pleasure to be external to the present enduring pain, that's the assumption of sensuality, isn't it?

864
00:52:48,280 --> 00:52:49,360
[kc]: Isn't like the... [??]

865
00:52:49,360 --> 00:52:50,273
[tn]: [??]

866
00:52:50,270 --> 00:52:51,554
[kc]: you can get rid of it, or something.

867
00:52:51,550 --> 00:52:52,014
[nm]: Sorry?

868
00:52:52,010 --> 00:52:52,650
[kc]: You can't, isn't it.

869
00:52:52,650 --> 00:52:53,830
[kc]: That's already implied, isn't it?

870
00:52:53,830 --> 00:52:54,888
[tn]: Or it's not connected.

871
00:52:56,250 --> 00:52:56,937
[nm]: Well, that's the thing.

872
00:52:57,170 --> 00:53:02,628
[nm]: Assuming being external to the pain, you already form the external relationship between the two.

873
00:53:02,620 --> 00:53:10,445
[nm]: Then, you can say it's before, it's after, it's not connected, it's fully connected, it's the same, it's different, it's both, it's neither, because you already assumed.

874
00:53:10,485 --> 00:53:17,591
[kc]: The point is, so that it... but basically, it's more that you want that... you assume that that pleasure

875
00:53:18,928 --> 00:53:19,920
[kc]: can get rid of that pain.

876
00:53:20,200 --> 00:53:23,725
[kc]: But that's because, more fundamentally, you see it as external from that pain.

877
00:53:24,220 --> 00:53:25,597
[kc]: And if you see that that pleasure...

878
00:53:25,911 --> 00:53:26,254
[nm]: Yeah.

879
00:53:26,250 --> 00:53:32,130
[kc]: It cannot possibly get rid of that pain, because it... because it isn't separate from that pain.

880
00:53:32,330 --> 00:53:33,200
[nm]: It's within, it's within.

881
00:53:33,200 --> 00:53:33,860
[nm]: It's always within.

882
00:53:33,860 --> 00:53:34,285
[kc]: Yeah, yeah.

883
00:53:34,748 --> 00:53:39,702
[nm]: In the same sense, you will stop maintaining the notion of your master controller of the five aggregates,

884
00:53:40,631 --> 00:53:46,145
[nm]: when you realize that any notion you can have about it, of sense of self and master and controller, it is within the five aggregates.

885
00:53:46,560 --> 00:53:54,942
[nm]: So, any notion of escape from this presently enduring pain, any notion of pleasure, any thought of: ah, tomorrow I'll experience this... It's within this.

886
00:53:55,068 --> 00:53:58,188
[nm]: So, at that time, to that extent, that is painful.

887
00:53:59,831 --> 00:54:03,297
[nm]: Which is why a prospect of going away from it is pleasant at the same time.

888
00:54:05,585 --> 00:54:11,417
[nm]: It's not like, again, you don't have to wait tomorrow to say no to yourself in regard to sense objects.

889
00:54:12,750 --> 00:54:15,090
[nm]: You can already do it right here, right now, on the level of the mind.

890
00:54:15,097 --> 00:54:16,845
[nm]: That's why sensuality is in the mind.

891
00:54:17,910 --> 00:54:22,260
[nm]: The Buddha gave that symbol, like a man lives completely immersed in sensuality.

892
00:54:22,260 --> 00:54:28,474
[nm]: It's like a man in the river, drenched, soaked, soaking wet, and then he finds two sticks and he wants to light the fire.

893
00:54:28,888 --> 00:54:33,002
[nm]: Well, first he needs to step outside of the river, because he can't light the fire with wet sticks.

894
00:54:33,560 --> 00:54:36,877
[nm]: But then, even when he's up on the shore, he won't be able to light the fire right away,

895
00:54:36,870 --> 00:54:40,017
[nm]: he needs to wait for sticks to dry, for his hands to dry.

896
00:54:40,530 --> 00:54:45,725
[nm]: And he said, so it's like the men who... monks who withdraw from sensuality, but their minds are still wet.

897
00:54:46,750 --> 00:54:50,571
[nm]: But when that dries, then you can... and lighting the fire basically means understanding this.

898
00:54:51,742 --> 00:54:55,080
[nm]: And then, yeah, he can't get wet again, because he's burnt up.

899
00:54:56,874 --> 00:54:57,431
[nm]: But that's the point.

900
00:54:57,430 --> 00:55:08,071
[nm]: So, like, now nothing, you're just kind of generally mindful, you don't have necessarily context of sensual assumptions, and you have a thought of something sensual, that you are about to be subjected to, or could be subjected to.

901
00:55:09,220 --> 00:55:13,251
[nm]: The delight, the extent of that delight, is the extent of your resistance to pain.

902
00:55:13,705 --> 00:55:14,271
[nm]: Nothing else.

903
00:55:15,250 --> 00:55:17,862
[nm]: The extent of that delight is not in the object that you don't have yet.

904
00:55:18,514 --> 00:55:21,451
[nm]: The extent of that delight is the extent of the pain, basically.

905
00:55:22,637 --> 00:55:23,034
[nm]: That's it.

906
00:55:26,900 --> 00:55:31,885
[nm]: And then, yeah, once the skin heals, scratching it, that's unpleasant.

907
00:55:33,280 --> 00:55:38,697
[nm]: So, it's the same act of the same sensuality, that was felt pleasantly first, because of an underlying condition.

908
00:55:39,097 --> 00:55:45,982
[nm]: So, you put underlying condition aside, an act of scratching is how... how is it felt then?

909
00:55:46,628 --> 00:55:47,574
[nm]: It's always unpleasant.

910
00:55:49,077 --> 00:55:53,574
[nm]: So, experience of sense objects is always unpleasant.

911
00:55:53,890 --> 00:55:55,274
[nm]: You're always harassed by it.

912
00:55:56,540 --> 00:55:57,440
[nm]: And again, that's what the Buddha said.

913
00:55:57,442 --> 00:55:58,211
[nm]: The simile of the cow.

914
00:55:58,240 --> 00:55:58,911
[nm]: Yeah, exactly.

915
00:55:58,950 --> 00:56:06,202
[nm]: The cow being... whether it leans on the wall, on the tree, sits down, stands, is being consumed by the insect that live in that... on that surface.

916
00:56:07,071 --> 00:56:08,094
[nm]: And that is always.

917
00:56:11,994 --> 00:56:14,808
[nm]: And that's why sensuality, as an attitude, grows.

918
00:56:15,145 --> 00:56:19,591
[nm]: The more you engage with it, the more options you get from it.

919
00:56:22,180 --> 00:56:25,034
[nm]: Because it's, again, it always stays with you, never, it can never leave that domain.

920
00:56:25,560 --> 00:56:30,577
[nm]: There is no outside of the sense objects.

921
00:56:30,951 --> 00:56:35,060
[nm]: Again, we spoke about it in regard to the form, but it's the same principle.

922
00:56:39,214 --> 00:56:41,220
[nm]: If you're touching something, what are you experiencing?

923
00:56:42,390 --> 00:56:45,750
[nm]: The object you're touching, or you're experiencing the experience of your hand touching something.

924
00:56:45,750 --> 00:56:46,430
[kc]: Exactly, yeah.

925
00:56:46,430 --> 00:56:46,662
[nm]: Exactly.

926
00:56:46,660 --> 00:57:01,442
[nm]: So, yet, here you are assuming that pleasure is contained in particular, inside of the particular objects that you can't even enter with your own senses, let alone on the level of the mind, somehow, to kind of transcend this domain and enter this domain of physicality.

927
00:57:01,500 --> 00:57:02,671
[nm]: It's inconceivable.

928
00:57:06,500 --> 00:57:08,910
[tn]: [?As] inconceivable that it's desire.

929
00:57:10,510 --> 00:57:11,420
[nm]: Yeah, the discrepancy...

930
00:57:11,420 --> 00:57:13,880
[tn]: By maintaining a desire, you're satisfying it.

931
00:57:15,942 --> 00:57:17,368
[tn]: Simultaneous. Yeah.

932
00:57:17,740 --> 00:57:18,914
[tn]: Then I'm going to satisfy it.

933
00:57:19,040 --> 00:57:23,428
[tn]: I'm going to keep this thing growing, and it's not going to... it's going to disappear.

934
00:57:23,631 --> 00:57:27,471
[nm]: Yeah, but it's going to disappear by becoming more and more apparent, yeah.

935
00:57:28,370 --> 00:57:29,094
[nm]: We're getting bigger.

936
00:57:35,280 --> 00:57:39,111
[nm]: So, when you do have... again, as I said, everybody starts from a wrong place first...

937
00:57:39,550 --> 00:57:45,062
[nm]: When you do have a thought of sensual object, don't try to negate it or deny it.

938
00:57:45,771 --> 00:57:48,488
[nm]: First, don't act towards it, which would be overly affirming it.

939
00:57:49,430 --> 00:57:51,128
[nm]: But now, don't try to deny it either.

940
00:57:51,480 --> 00:57:52,410
[nm]: Allow it to endure.

941
00:57:52,410 --> 00:57:52,730
[nm]: Why?

942
00:57:52,730 --> 00:57:56,788
[nm]: Because that's how you can discern a context greater than the thought of sensuality.

943
00:57:59,162 --> 00:58:00,410
[nm]: And this is the context greater.

944
00:58:00,410 --> 00:58:01,062
[nm]: We just described it.

945
00:58:01,060 --> 00:58:02,588
[nm]: So, oh, I... there is again...

946
00:58:03,160 --> 00:58:03,642
[nm]: I don't know.

947
00:58:03,740 --> 00:58:06,174
[nm]: I'm hungry and there is a nice food on the table.

948
00:58:07,345 --> 00:58:09,231
[nm]: And there is a delightful prospect.

949
00:58:09,230 --> 00:58:10,362
[nm]: I'm delighting in it.

950
00:58:11,388 --> 00:58:12,470
[nm]: I'm not acting out of it.

951
00:58:13,042 --> 00:58:16,342
[nm]: So, I'm practicing restraint, but the delight is there.

952
00:58:16,410 --> 00:58:18,291
[nm]: But if I'm like: oh, I shouldn't feel this, I shouldn't feel it.

953
00:58:18,290 --> 00:58:20,280
[nm]: Mean: oh, now I still, I'm trying to get rid of it.

954
00:58:20,782 --> 00:58:22,154
[nm]: First, I try to go for it.

955
00:58:22,188 --> 00:58:23,328
[nm]: Now, I try to go against it.

956
00:58:23,320 --> 00:58:25,005
[nm]: Either way, I want to get rid of it.

957
00:58:25,920 --> 00:58:27,617
[nm]: So, you must stop trying to get rid of it.

958
00:58:28,165 --> 00:58:35,562
[nm]: So, once you stop... once you start restraining and don't, as I said, overly affirming to your physical action, you do have to learn how to allow it to endure.

959
00:58:35,820 --> 00:58:37,007
[nm]: Not mentally: I don't want it.

960
00:58:37,000 --> 00:58:37,880
[nm]: I don't want it.

961
00:58:38,334 --> 00:58:40,011
[nm]: Because you didn't create it to begin with.

962
00:58:40,010 --> 00:58:40,925
[nm]: You're subjected to it.

963
00:58:41,180 --> 00:58:43,768
[nm]: And your only freedom from what you're subjected to is to fully understand it.

964
00:58:43,788 --> 00:58:45,670
[nm]: You can't understand it if you keep denying it.

965
00:58:47,065 --> 00:58:52,285
[nm]: So, food is on the table, I'm very hungry, but I'm restraining myself, it hasn't been offered, I'm not gonna eat it.

966
00:58:52,768 --> 00:58:57,340
[nm]: Now I have the delight in my mind, the prospect of eating it, the prospect of somebody coming and offering me, and I'm eating it, and so on.

967
00:58:59,588 --> 00:59:00,720
[nm]: How do you free yourself from that?

968
00:59:02,331 --> 00:59:07,374
[nm]: Or how do you regain perspective in regard to that directional prospect?

969
00:59:10,991 --> 00:59:13,277
[nm]: As I said, would you be eating the food?

970
00:59:13,430 --> 00:59:14,260
[kc]: No. First of all... 

971
00:59:14,260 --> 00:59:17,382
[nm]: Or would you be experiencing your mouth being subjected to food?

972
00:59:20,330 --> 00:59:23,880
[nm]: And, see, that's the context that you can easily ignore.

973
00:59:25,400 --> 00:59:38,494
[nm]: But you realize, if you make an effort to not ignore it, you would actually shift the emphasis from the food, food, food, food, to, oh, these random senses that I was given, subjected to, are then subjected to further things.

974
00:59:39,310 --> 00:59:49,440
[nm]: Even if those things are agreeable or disagreeable, you stop fearing them, because now you're at the right basis of not being careless in regard to the... As I said, can you experience the food?

975
00:59:49,660 --> 00:59:53,220
[nm]: Can you experience any sense object if your senses are not there operating, living?

976
00:59:53,362 --> 00:59:55,351
[nm]: If there is no sixth sense base present?

977
00:59:56,128 --> 00:59:57,822
[nm]: If the body is not there functional?

978
00:59:58,085 --> 00:59:58,657
[nm]: You can't.

979
00:59:58,948 --> 00:59:59,570
[nm]: Impossible.

980
01:00:00,051 --> 01:00:02,497
[nm]: So you realize, it doesn't matter how much I forget this,

981
01:00:03,322 --> 01:00:04,608
[nm]: It is the right order of things.

982
01:00:04,600 --> 01:00:05,510
[nm]: The body comes first.

983
01:00:05,510 --> 01:00:08,422
[nm]: The necessity of the six senses comes first.

984
01:00:08,968 --> 01:00:21,457
[nm]: Yeah, they're only known through engagement with sense objects, but, again, I cannot abandon them to go to sense objects, because my only formal relationship is within them that relate to sense objects.

985
01:00:21,637 --> 01:00:24,091
[nm]: So, you stop assuming external to your six senses.

986
01:00:24,371 --> 01:00:25,854
[nm]: Again, upādāna undone.

987
01:00:26,220 --> 01:00:29,870
[nm]: You stop assuming external to the sense of five aggregate, attavāda undone.

988
01:00:30,770 --> 01:00:34,442
[nm]: You stop assuming external to the basically presently enduring feeling.

989
01:00:35,317 --> 01:00:40,690
[nm]: Means you stop craving against the presently enduring feeling, whether against the words or against the way from it.

990
01:00:41,162 --> 01:00:42,091
[nm]: Upādāna, I'm done.

991
01:00:43,888 --> 01:00:44,950
[nm]: It's always the same principle.

992
01:00:44,950 --> 01:00:46,200
[nm]: That's why it's always upādāna.

